1
00:00:14,014 --> 00:00:17,984
A makeover project
for your most unhinged leftovers.

2
00:00:18,051 --> 00:00:21,454
The best chefs in Korea will
turn your fridge inside out.

3
00:00:21,521 --> 00:00:23,823
The classy cooking show has returned.

4
00:00:23,890 --> 00:00:27,027
<i>-Chef & My Fridge!</i>
<i>-My Fridge!</i>

5
00:00:27,093 --> 00:00:28,695
Hello.

6
00:00:29,195 --> 00:00:31,698
STARTING ANOTHER EPISODE WITH GREAT ENERGY

7
00:00:31,765 --> 00:00:35,635
We're here today
with a webtoon artist and a director

8
00:00:35,702 --> 00:00:38,872
-sitting side by side.
-It's time for the unorthodox clan

9
00:00:38,938 --> 00:00:41,808
-to slowly take over.
-There are too many of them.

10
00:00:41,875 --> 00:00:44,677
-You've now taken up two spots.
-Exactly.

11
00:00:44,744 --> 00:00:46,546
-Let's pull it together.
-I should find another show.

12
00:00:46,613 --> 00:00:49,382
Is anxiety more prevalent
because of this new movement?

13
00:00:49,449 --> 00:00:50,884
One of the chefs

14
00:00:50,950 --> 00:00:53,386
had something they really had to say.

15
00:00:53,453 --> 00:00:55,955
-They wrote us a handwritten letter.
-A handwritten letter?

16
00:00:56,022 --> 00:00:57,190
A HANDWRITTEN LETTER?

17
00:00:57,257 --> 00:00:59,759
-Who was it?
-Let me read the letter we got,

18
00:00:59,826 --> 00:01:01,528
word for word.

19
00:01:01,594 --> 00:01:05,465
"Chef Sung-jun, you recently realized
how popular you were in Hong Kong?"

20
00:01:05,532 --> 00:01:06,366
What is this about?

21
00:01:06,433 --> 00:01:09,269
-Is he asking you to ask that?
-It's for us to ask him.

22
00:01:09,335 --> 00:01:11,071
-It's a question.
-He wrote that himself?

23
00:01:11,371 --> 00:01:13,673
A HANDWRITTEN LETTER
FULL OF DESIRE TO FLAUNT

24
00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:15,775
He asked us to ask this, so I'll do it.

25
00:01:15,842 --> 00:01:18,778
"Chef Sung-jun, you recently realized
how popular you were in Hong Kong?"

26
00:01:20,013 --> 00:01:20,847
FISHING FOR COMPLIMENTS

27
00:01:20,914 --> 00:01:21,981
What was that like?

28
00:01:22,048 --> 00:01:24,617
-I went to Hong Kong last week.
-I see.

29
00:01:24,684 --> 00:01:26,619
And both the show
and I were incredibly popular.

30
00:01:26,886 --> 00:01:28,488
THROWING HIMSELF IN THERE

31
00:01:28,555 --> 00:01:30,090
I held an event there,

32
00:01:30,156 --> 00:01:32,325
and about 200 to 300 people showed up.

33
00:01:32,392 --> 00:01:35,095
I ended up taking
thousands of pictures with them.

34
00:01:35,161 --> 00:01:37,564
-Thousands of photos with 200, 300 people?
-How does it add up?

35
00:01:37,630 --> 00:01:40,567
-They must've taken ten each.
-They wanted ten each.

36
00:01:40,633 --> 00:01:42,302
-We usually count that as one.
-Also,

37
00:01:42,368 --> 00:01:44,070
they asked me to do things like,

38
00:01:44,137 --> 00:01:47,173
"It's an emergency" or "Miss."

39
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:48,475
THIS?

40
00:01:48,541 --> 00:01:50,143
-Miss.
-They even know what Korean fans don't?

41
00:01:50,210 --> 00:01:51,344
Only I've been doing it.

42
00:01:51,411 --> 00:01:53,213
-Impossible.
-Only we do it to play along.

43
00:01:53,279 --> 00:01:54,180
To humor him.

44
00:01:54,247 --> 00:01:56,916
I guess he looks like
he could be an actor in Hong Kong.

45
00:01:56,983 --> 00:01:58,885
Yes, I think my looks are their type.

46
00:01:58,952 --> 00:01:59,853
-Sammo Hung.
-Sammo Hung.

47
00:01:59,919 --> 00:02:01,488
-Sammo Hung.
-He's like Sammo Hung.

48
00:02:01,554 --> 00:02:03,857
He has a face
that Hong Kongers don't really like.

49
00:02:03,923 --> 00:02:06,226
-They don't like his face?
-That's right.

50
00:02:06,292 --> 00:02:08,328
-He's not their type.
-What do you know, Amy?

51
00:02:08,394 --> 00:02:09,729
-Is there an overhype?
-Yes.

52
00:02:09,796 --> 00:02:11,531
I believe the overhype is quite serious.

53
00:02:11,598 --> 00:02:14,868
-So what he said was exaggerated.
-It was exaggerated.

54
00:02:14,934 --> 00:02:17,770
There's somebody else
who claimed something similar.

55
00:02:17,837 --> 00:02:19,305
"Chef Jong-won.

56
00:02:19,372 --> 00:02:21,941
I hear you were quite popular in Taiwan."

57
00:02:22,008 --> 00:02:23,476
-This is true.
-It's true.

58
00:02:23,543 --> 00:02:24,444
This one, I can believe it.

59
00:02:24,511 --> 00:02:26,346
-Why is this true?
-Is this also true?

60
00:02:26,412 --> 00:02:29,516
I went to Taiwan
for this very private event,

61
00:02:29,582 --> 00:02:31,718
and hundreds of people showed up,
so I was surprised.

62
00:02:31,784 --> 00:02:34,521
I heard the show
has been airing on their TV,

63
00:02:34,587 --> 00:02:35,855
<i>and our chefs are popular there.</i>

64
00:02:35,922 --> 00:02:37,490
I'M TELLING YOU

65
00:02:37,557 --> 00:02:38,825
I know I shouldn't be like this,

66
00:02:38,892 --> 00:02:41,161
but why does everything he say sound true?

67
00:02:42,128 --> 00:02:44,631
-Right? Let's not be like that.
-That's true.

68
00:02:44,697 --> 00:02:46,299
Is there proof?

69
00:02:46,366 --> 00:02:49,202
You don't have to provide any.
We already have it.

70
00:02:49,269 --> 00:02:52,005
See? These pictures are available.

71
00:02:52,071 --> 00:02:53,439
WHY NOT MY PICTURES?

72
00:02:53,506 --> 00:02:54,707
The picture's out there.

73
00:02:54,774 --> 00:02:56,342
WOW

74
00:02:56,409 --> 00:02:58,411
The picture's out there.

75
00:02:58,478 --> 00:03:00,180
-Whoa!
-That's a lot.

76
00:03:00,246 --> 00:03:01,848
Look at the second floor.

77
00:03:01,915 --> 00:03:03,049
My crowd was bigger.

78
00:03:03,116 --> 00:03:04,417
I had a bigger crowd.

79
00:03:04,484 --> 00:03:05,618
Where are you, Jong-won?

80
00:03:05,685 --> 00:03:09,355
-Right? Jong-won isn't in the picture.
-He's not.

81
00:03:09,923 --> 00:03:11,157
IS THIS PHOTO REAL?

82
00:03:11,224 --> 00:03:13,726
-You're right!
-He's not in the picture.

83
00:03:13,793 --> 00:03:14,827
JONG-WON'S PHOTO WITHOUT HIM

84
00:03:14,894 --> 00:03:17,130
Some even say
I'm the one who took the photo.

85
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:18,498
A SELF-TAKEN PHOTO(?)

86
00:03:18,565 --> 00:03:19,566
I knew it.

87
00:03:19,832 --> 00:03:21,668
TAIWANESE FANS,
PLEASE SHOW US PHOTOGRAPHIC PROOF♥

88
00:03:21,734 --> 00:03:24,437
There's another one. "Chef Ho-young.

89
00:03:24,504 --> 00:03:27,840
You went to Taiwan
and finally felt how popular you were."

90
00:03:27,907 --> 00:03:29,642
You don't seem to believe it.

91
00:03:29,709 --> 00:03:30,643
So this was how you all felt?

92
00:03:30,710 --> 00:03:32,745
I've seen it already.
It's on his social media.

93
00:03:32,812 --> 00:03:34,581
He uploaded pictures right away

94
00:03:34,647 --> 00:03:36,883
-on his social media account.
-He did?

95
00:03:36,950 --> 00:03:38,318
-Everyone recognized him.
-He won't hold back.

96
00:03:38,384 --> 00:03:39,619
He won't hold back.

97
00:03:39,686 --> 00:03:40,787
THE ADDICT CAN'T HELP IT

98
00:03:40,853 --> 00:03:41,788
I got lots of likes.

99
00:03:41,854 --> 00:03:43,623
He told me then

100
00:03:43,690 --> 00:03:46,359
that he couldn't even
walk down the street.

101
00:03:46,426 --> 00:03:47,927
-Maybe his legs were hurting.
-Ho-young?

102
00:03:47,994 --> 00:03:49,095
Was the street too narrow?

103
00:03:49,162 --> 00:03:51,331
Was the weather just too hot to walk?

104
00:03:51,397 --> 00:03:54,133
-Well, it was hot.
-Let's see how it was for him.

105
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:55,868
Let's see if many people showed up.

106
00:03:58,204 --> 00:03:59,772
-That's a lot.
-Impressive.

107
00:03:59,839 --> 00:04:00,873
AMAZED

108
00:04:01,507 --> 00:04:03,710
It looks photoshopped.

109
00:04:03,776 --> 00:04:05,745
-His face looks too slim.
-The shadow looks odd.

110
00:04:05,812 --> 00:04:07,680
-That's not him.
-It's suspicious.

111
00:04:07,747 --> 00:04:09,148
Oh, that's AI-generated.

112
00:04:09,415 --> 00:04:10,850
SUSPICIONS OF AI USAGE

113
00:04:10,917 --> 00:04:12,919
You were cut out from another photo.

114
00:04:12,986 --> 00:04:14,887
<i>Yes, something's odd.</i>

115
00:04:14,954 --> 00:04:16,456
<i>-It's AI-generated.</i>
<i>-It must be.</i>

116
00:04:16,522 --> 00:04:18,257
-It wasn't photoshopped, right?
-No.

117
00:04:18,324 --> 00:04:19,892
SHOW US PROOF, TAIWANESE FANS♥

118
00:04:19,959 --> 00:04:21,928
Now, another chef

119
00:04:21,995 --> 00:04:25,365
decided to turn in
material evidence, not just a photo.

120
00:04:25,431 --> 00:04:29,469
"Chef Hyun-suk.
I heard you visited Singapore."

121
00:04:29,535 --> 00:04:32,105
-Did you bring something?
-What's that?

122
00:04:32,171 --> 00:04:33,706
Did he get us souvenirs?

123
00:04:34,140 --> 00:04:35,308
HANDS SOMETHING OVER

124
00:04:35,375 --> 00:04:36,843
He got these presents.

125
00:04:36,909 --> 00:04:38,278
PRESENTS FROM FANS

126
00:04:39,779 --> 00:04:43,016
Lots of identical plushies.
Are these from a claw machine?

127
00:04:43,082 --> 00:04:46,486
<i>I was told to give it to other chefs.</i>
<i>Their names are on the tags.</i>

128
00:04:46,552 --> 00:04:48,488
AND A NOTE IN KOREAN♥

129
00:04:48,554 --> 00:04:50,189
<i>We'll hand these out to everyone.</i>

130
00:04:50,256 --> 00:04:52,792
And someone asked you
to sign their perfume bottle?

131
00:04:52,859 --> 00:04:55,595
They brought a bottle
labeled "Senior No. 55"

132
00:04:55,662 --> 00:04:58,197
<i>-and asked me to sign it.</i>
<i>-They watched the episode.</i>

133
00:04:58,264 --> 00:05:00,566
-All the details.
-They know everything.

134
00:05:00,633 --> 00:05:03,603
-What's this tiger balm?
-Tiger balm.

135
00:05:03,670 --> 00:05:05,972
It's in the pain plaster form.

136
00:05:06,039 --> 00:05:06,873
<i>How convenient.</i>

137
00:05:06,939 --> 00:05:08,941
Because your shoulders hurt when salting?

138
00:05:09,008 --> 00:05:10,476
They watched everything in detail.

139
00:05:10,543 --> 00:05:13,813
Fan letters used say, "Always be happy"
or "May only good things come your way."

140
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:14,714
But these days,

141
00:05:14,781 --> 00:05:18,051
<i>it usually says, "Please stay healthy."</i>

142
00:05:18,117 --> 00:05:20,920
<i>It says in Korean,</i>
<i>"Happy birthday, Grandpa!"</i>

143
00:05:20,987 --> 00:05:22,322
When was your birthday?

144
00:05:22,889 --> 00:05:23,756
It's today.

145
00:05:23,823 --> 00:05:25,758
What? Today's your birthday?

146
00:05:26,159 --> 00:05:28,027
IT SEEMS THAT NOBODY KNEW…

147
00:05:28,094 --> 00:05:30,897
I should spend my birthday with my family,

148
00:05:30,963 --> 00:05:33,866
but I'm here shooting this show,
coughing up blood.

149
00:05:33,933 --> 00:05:36,269
If he's coughing up blood,
he shouldn't have come.

150
00:05:36,336 --> 00:05:39,372
I've now truly become Senior No. 55.

151
00:05:39,439 --> 00:05:42,342
You're now 55 years old, legally.

152
00:05:42,575 --> 00:05:44,143
THE BEST AGE IN LIFE, 55

153
00:05:44,210 --> 00:05:47,013
Always stay healthy, and happy birthday.

154
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:50,516
Now, let's welcome today's guests.

155
00:05:50,583 --> 00:05:52,819
We present

156
00:05:52,885 --> 00:05:55,021
today's fridge owners. Come on out!

157
00:05:57,090 --> 00:05:59,025
Today's fridge owners are

158
00:05:59,092 --> 00:06:01,327
Uhm Jung-hwa and Choi Sooyoung!

159
00:06:01,394 --> 00:06:02,328
Welcome to the show.

160
00:06:04,964 --> 00:06:07,667
-Hello.
-Please come and have a seat.

161
00:06:07,734 --> 00:06:09,135
They're beautiful.

162
00:06:09,202 --> 00:06:13,639
You two just made
the fanciest entrance in our history.

163
00:06:13,706 --> 00:06:16,442
Please allow me to introduce her first.

164
00:06:16,509 --> 00:06:18,745
We've been waiting for her to visit us.

165
00:06:18,811 --> 00:06:20,546
A simply Uhmazing star

166
00:06:20,613 --> 00:06:22,749
with an amazing discography
and filmography,

167
00:06:22,815 --> 00:06:24,617
please welcome Uhm Jung-hwa!

168
00:06:24,684 --> 00:06:25,952
AN UHMAZING GUEST

169
00:06:26,018 --> 00:06:27,820
Hello, everyone.

170
00:06:27,887 --> 00:06:29,756
I'm finally here!

171
00:06:33,192 --> 00:06:34,761
Let's introduce our next guest.

172
00:06:34,827 --> 00:06:37,530
There is a chef
whose wish was to have her on the show.

173
00:06:37,597 --> 00:06:39,999
-There is one.
-Yes, there is.

174
00:06:40,066 --> 00:06:42,101
-Please welcome Sooyoung!
-Sooyoung!

175
00:06:42,168 --> 00:06:43,903
-Hello.
-Hello.

176
00:06:44,170 --> 00:06:46,372
BLUSHING DOUGH GUY

177
00:06:46,439 --> 00:06:49,642
I hear there's a reason
why you two came here together.

178
00:06:49,709 --> 00:06:52,578
-Our film is premiering soon.
-A film.

179
00:06:52,645 --> 00:06:55,681
It's called <i>Okay! Madam 2.</i>
The second in the franchise.

180
00:06:55,748 --> 00:06:57,116
-The second film.
-Yes.

181
00:06:57,183 --> 00:07:00,353
<i>The first film</i>
<i>centered around plane hijacking,</i>

182
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:02,121
but this time, we're on a cruise.

183
00:07:02,188 --> 00:07:05,091
<i>-A cruise ship?</i>
<i>-Yes, I run into enemies on the ship.</i>

184
00:07:05,158 --> 00:07:06,926
-Me.
-You're her enemy?

185
00:07:06,993 --> 00:07:08,895
-You're the enemy?
-I'm the villain.

186
00:07:09,128 --> 00:07:10,163
IT'S ME, THE VILLAIN

187
00:07:10,229 --> 00:07:12,331
<i>You'll see awesome action scenes</i>

188
00:07:12,398 --> 00:07:15,001
<i>and take a tour</i>
<i>around every corner of the cruise ship.</i>

189
00:07:15,067 --> 00:07:17,036
-It premieres on August 12th.
-August 12th.

190
00:07:17,103 --> 00:07:18,604
-Yes.
-All right.

191
00:07:18,671 --> 00:07:21,474
It already sounds exhilarating,
<i>Okay! Madam 2.</i>

192
00:07:21,541 --> 00:07:25,211
Jung-hwa, did you say you felt like
you came to the show to meet celebrities?

193
00:07:25,278 --> 00:07:27,480
I've been watching the show

194
00:07:27,547 --> 00:07:29,115
since it began.

195
00:07:29,182 --> 00:07:30,683
I love the way

196
00:07:30,750 --> 00:07:33,386
the chefs create these witty dishes,

197
00:07:33,453 --> 00:07:36,355
so I've been dying to meet everyone.

198
00:07:36,422 --> 00:07:38,357
You've singled out a few people

199
00:07:38,424 --> 00:07:40,893
who actually make the show hilarious.

200
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:43,229
WHICH ONES?

201
00:07:43,296 --> 00:07:45,631
It's Sung-ju and Jung-hwan.

202
00:07:45,698 --> 00:07:46,766
Us?

203
00:07:46,833 --> 00:07:48,768
It's when you go and have a taste.

204
00:07:48,835 --> 00:07:50,136
You go, "Will it fly?"

205
00:07:50,203 --> 00:07:51,204
And he goes, "It won't fly!"

206
00:07:51,604 --> 00:07:52,672
THE HYPER Q&A SESH

207
00:07:52,738 --> 00:07:54,607
Will the dish give more energy?

208
00:07:54,674 --> 00:07:55,842
It's too salty!

209
00:07:55,908 --> 00:07:57,009
It's too sweet!

210
00:07:57,076 --> 00:07:58,478
ON TOP OF THAT…

211
00:07:58,544 --> 00:08:00,613
HE EVEN GETS POSSESSED
DURING THE 5-MINUTE CHECK

212
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:02,281
You two are hilarious.

213
00:08:02,348 --> 00:08:05,051
She's the first guest
to compliment the hosts.

214
00:08:05,251 --> 00:08:06,786
KUDOS TO THE HOSTS

215
00:08:07,286 --> 00:08:08,688
THEY'RE SO EXCITED…

216
00:08:08,754 --> 00:08:12,558
Sooyoung should've joined us
much earlier than this.

217
00:08:12,625 --> 00:08:15,895
There's someone here who's been
waiting forever for you to come.

218
00:08:15,962 --> 00:08:17,864
Chef Sung-jun.

219
00:08:17,930 --> 00:08:19,532
Back when Yoona was on the show…

220
00:08:19,599 --> 00:08:22,902
While I was an active member of a fansite,
I was nicknamed Sooyoung's Hubby.

221
00:08:22,969 --> 00:08:24,770
-My gosh!
-That's right.

222
00:08:24,837 --> 00:08:27,740
You watched the episode
and even uploaded a post about it.

223
00:08:27,807 --> 00:08:28,941
-I did.
-Yes.

224
00:08:29,008 --> 00:08:31,577
I was really happy to see that.

225
00:08:31,644 --> 00:08:33,279
Stop being so happy.

226
00:08:33,346 --> 00:08:35,948
She's finally here with us.
How do you feel?

227
00:08:36,015 --> 00:08:37,717
First, let me greet her.

228
00:08:37,783 --> 00:08:39,519
I am Kwon Sung-jun, a chef.

229
00:08:40,553 --> 00:08:41,621
What was that?

230
00:08:41,687 --> 00:08:43,089
What's he doing?

231
00:08:43,155 --> 00:08:44,690
-Jeez.
-He's embarrassing me.

232
00:08:45,057 --> 00:08:47,360
IT WAS LIKE
A BOTCHED FIRST LINE AT A BLIND DATE…

233
00:08:47,426 --> 00:08:48,861
THAT WAS THE WORST

234
00:08:48,928 --> 00:08:50,496
My heart is racing too fast today.

235
00:08:50,563 --> 00:08:53,299
He's flushed. Wait, his ears are so red!

236
00:08:53,366 --> 00:08:54,667
-What's with you?
-What's with you?

237
00:08:54,734 --> 00:08:56,502
I can't look at her.

238
00:08:56,569 --> 00:08:57,703
Oh, gosh.

239
00:08:58,371 --> 00:09:00,606
Back then, I didn't have many fans

240
00:09:00,673 --> 00:09:02,241
who supported me.

241
00:09:02,308 --> 00:09:03,409
No way.

242
00:09:03,476 --> 00:09:06,345
Taeyeon, Tiffany, and Yoona

243
00:09:06,412 --> 00:09:08,447
were the ones with lots of fans.

244
00:09:08,514 --> 00:09:09,782
I had so few fans

245
00:09:09,849 --> 00:09:11,817
that I'd remember all their usernames.

246
00:09:11,884 --> 00:09:14,287
I'm sure you had a reason
for having her as your bias.

247
00:09:14,353 --> 00:09:16,789
Yes, I've been wanting
to ask you the reason.

248
00:09:16,856 --> 00:09:19,191
Well, I'm someone who has short limbs,

249
00:09:19,258 --> 00:09:22,028
-so I like people with long limbs.
-And hers are long.

250
00:09:22,094 --> 00:09:24,463
Also, she has her own little flair
when she dances.

251
00:09:24,530 --> 00:09:25,831
-What is it?
-She flips her hair.

252
00:09:27,934 --> 00:09:29,101
LIKE THIS

253
00:09:29,168 --> 00:09:30,870
What's that? A hair flair?

254
00:09:30,937 --> 00:09:33,439
I have this thing I do when I dance.

255
00:09:33,506 --> 00:09:34,774
I tend to flip my hair a lot.

256
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:36,909
-Show us.
-Others do it normally.

257
00:09:36,976 --> 00:09:38,411
-She's up.
-You're so pretty.

258
00:09:38,477 --> 00:09:39,445
But I go…

259
00:09:39,512 --> 00:09:40,546
HAHA…

260
00:09:40,613 --> 00:09:42,448
SUDDENLY FEELS CRINGY

261
00:09:42,515 --> 00:09:44,183
She's suddenly hit with a moment.

262
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:45,918
-You can do this!
-You got this!

263
00:09:46,118 --> 00:09:47,420
YOU CAN DO IT

264
00:09:47,486 --> 00:09:48,654
Ready, go.

265
00:09:49,956 --> 00:09:51,524
FLIP

266
00:09:51,591 --> 00:09:53,125
STARTING WITH A HAIR FLIP

267
00:09:53,192 --> 00:09:54,026
CASCADING

268
00:09:54,327 --> 00:09:55,761
GREAT JOB

269
00:09:56,095 --> 00:09:57,463
AM I DOING A GREAT JOB?

270
00:09:57,897 --> 00:09:59,298
MOVE ASIDE, EVERYONE

271
00:09:59,732 --> 00:10:02,602
WE HOPE SUNG-JUN CAN BE
LESS HAPPY THAN HE IS NOW…

272
00:10:03,636 --> 00:10:04,937
HER HAIR FLIP CATCHES ATTENTION

273
00:10:05,004 --> 00:10:06,505
You're so beautiful.

274
00:10:06,572 --> 00:10:08,007
Your eyes end up getting drawn to her.

275
00:10:08,074 --> 00:10:09,775
These days, taller members

276
00:10:09,842 --> 00:10:13,245
don't always stand on the side.
Sometimes they even take the center.

277
00:10:13,312 --> 00:10:15,748
-Yes.
-But back then,

278
00:10:15,815 --> 00:10:18,317
<i>taller members usually stood</i>
<i>in the back, off to the side.</i>

279
00:10:18,384 --> 00:10:20,786
Yes, times have changed.

280
00:10:20,853 --> 00:10:23,589
It's better to have
the tallest person stand in the center.

281
00:10:23,656 --> 00:10:25,725
<i>If the tallest one is in the back row,</i>
<i>the perception is lost.</i>

282
00:10:25,791 --> 00:10:27,026
You're right.

283
00:10:27,093 --> 00:10:29,595
To stage a good performance,
it's better for long-limbed members…

284
00:10:29,662 --> 00:10:30,830
Look at her face.

285
00:10:30,896 --> 00:10:31,897
IN TOTAL AGREEMENT

286
00:10:31,964 --> 00:10:34,000
-She should've been in the center.
-Yes.

287
00:10:34,567 --> 00:10:36,769
When you plate your food, I'm sure you put

288
00:10:36,836 --> 00:10:38,838
-the longest piece in the middle.
-Yes.

289
00:10:38,904 --> 00:10:41,073
The center
is always reserved for the longest…

290
00:10:41,140 --> 00:10:43,976
-She knows what's up.
-Yes.

291
00:10:45,244 --> 00:10:46,545
They're a great duo.

292
00:10:46,812 --> 00:10:49,048
THE SHORT-LIMBED GUY IS DISPLEASED…

293
00:10:49,115 --> 00:10:50,850
The tallest person
should be in the middle.

294
00:10:50,916 --> 00:10:53,319
As soon as I saw Girls' Generation,

295
00:10:53,386 --> 00:10:54,453
I felt frustrated.

296
00:10:54,754 --> 00:10:56,022
OH, GOSH…

297
00:10:56,088 --> 00:10:58,391
Why is she back there?
She should be in the front.

298
00:10:58,457 --> 00:10:59,625
-Right?
-Yes.

299
00:10:59,692 --> 00:11:02,728
She should've shown
the impact of her hair flip

300
00:11:02,795 --> 00:11:05,898
in the very front
to let it flare out to the edges.

301
00:11:06,766 --> 00:11:08,034
When will he be done?

302
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:10,102
I'll… What were you doing?
Why didn't you protest?

303
00:11:10,169 --> 00:11:11,203
I'm sorry.

304
00:11:11,270 --> 00:11:13,139
You probably weren't a huge fan.

305
00:11:13,205 --> 00:11:14,540
-You should've…
-He faked it.

306
00:11:15,441 --> 00:11:17,543
Fans often protest with trucks these days.

307
00:11:18,210 --> 00:11:20,746
You should've sent one yourself.

308
00:11:20,813 --> 00:11:23,449
You should've demanded
that I stand in the center.

309
00:11:23,716 --> 00:11:25,751
SPEECHLESS…

310
00:11:25,818 --> 00:11:27,019
If Sooyoung was in the center,

311
00:11:27,086 --> 00:11:29,455
the impact of K-pop
in the world's history would've shifted.

312
00:11:29,522 --> 00:11:30,823
It would've changed.

313
00:11:30,890 --> 00:11:32,692
-She would've gone first.
-I would've.

314
00:11:32,758 --> 00:11:34,827
-I would've gone to Coachella.
-You would have!

315
00:11:35,127 --> 00:11:36,729
INTIMIDATED…

316
00:11:36,796 --> 00:11:39,331
Next year is our 20th anniversary,

317
00:11:39,398 --> 00:11:41,767
-so show me some support.
-Of course.

318
00:11:41,834 --> 00:11:43,969
I'll drive my car there and protest.

319
00:11:44,036 --> 00:11:46,639
A MODEST 1-PERSON PROTEST…

320
00:11:46,706 --> 00:11:48,774
I should've debuted again now.

321
00:11:49,775 --> 00:11:50,910
So you are.

322
00:11:50,976 --> 00:11:52,211
Yes, I am.

323
00:11:52,278 --> 00:11:54,246
I'M DEBUTING SOON

324
00:11:54,313 --> 00:11:55,648
-Girls' Generation-HRS.
-Yes.

325
00:11:55,715 --> 00:11:57,750
SHE'LL DEBUT AS A UNIT,
GIRLS' GENERATION-HRS

326
00:11:57,817 --> 00:12:00,219
Back when Hyo-yeon visited us,

327
00:12:00,286 --> 00:12:02,688
you were yet to start
your official promotion.

328
00:12:02,755 --> 00:12:05,191
Yes, but we gained lots of popularity,

329
00:12:05,257 --> 00:12:08,294
so we ended up making our actual debut.

330
00:12:10,062 --> 00:12:11,497
Why couldn't they change the name?

331
00:12:11,564 --> 00:12:13,165
Girls' Generation-SHR.

332
00:12:13,232 --> 00:12:14,800
-SHR? Or SRH.
-Girls' Generation-SRH.

333
00:12:14,867 --> 00:12:17,570
S for Sooyoung
should be in the very front.

334
00:12:17,636 --> 00:12:18,704
-I'm sorry.
-But it's…

335
00:12:18,771 --> 00:12:20,172
That was a bit of a stretch.

336
00:12:22,174 --> 00:12:24,043
That's a good one.

337
00:12:24,110 --> 00:12:27,646
That unit is already doing so well.

338
00:12:27,713 --> 00:12:31,317
I demanded that I be the center
for Girls' Generation-HRS,

339
00:12:31,383 --> 00:12:33,085
<i>but Hyo-yeon said…</i>

340
00:12:33,152 --> 00:12:34,620
You're like the middle finger.

341
00:12:36,422 --> 00:12:38,424
Right. Like the Chinese character
for mountain.

342
00:12:38,491 --> 00:12:40,092
COME TO THINK OF IT, MAYBE…

343
00:12:40,159 --> 00:12:41,694
Like the character for mountain.

344
00:12:41,761 --> 00:12:43,562
I've been getting pulled
in all directions.

345
00:12:44,797 --> 00:12:46,265
SAD FOR HER

346
00:12:46,332 --> 00:12:49,401
What's this song that gave you energy
whenever you were down?

347
00:12:49,468 --> 00:12:50,636
A song that gave you energy?

348
00:12:50,703 --> 00:12:53,005
-It's called "Rule of the Princess."
-"Rule of the Princess"?

349
00:12:53,072 --> 00:12:54,874
-"Rule of the Princess"?
-I've never heard of it.

350
00:12:54,940 --> 00:12:56,242
Not "Princess Is Lonely"?

351
00:12:56,308 --> 00:12:58,344
-"Princess Is Lonely."
-"Rule of the Princess"?

352
00:12:58,410 --> 00:13:00,112
It's about that strong princess spirit.

353
00:13:00,179 --> 00:13:01,080
That's nice.

354
00:13:01,147 --> 00:13:02,314
-I see.
-That's nice.

355
00:13:02,381 --> 00:13:03,516
Doesn't it make you emotional?

356
00:13:03,582 --> 00:13:06,418
-It does.
-It makes me feel like crying.

357
00:13:06,485 --> 00:13:08,053
She's connecting with the song.

358
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:10,055
She seemed impressed by the lyrics.

359
00:13:10,122 --> 00:13:11,524
This makes you emotional?

360
00:13:12,324 --> 00:13:13,225
Are you a type T?

361
00:13:13,492 --> 00:13:14,660
CAN'T RELATE…

362
00:13:15,294 --> 00:13:18,063
-"Don't chase the stars. Be a star."
-Live as a star.

363
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:21,634
Our chefs have been stressed out
with the heightened competition.

364
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:23,135
-It's tough.
-Sam?

365
00:13:23,202 --> 00:13:24,937
Did you just hear the lyrics?

366
00:13:25,004 --> 00:13:26,539
A TENACIOUS STAR-OBSESSED CHEF

367
00:13:26,605 --> 00:13:28,274
Fetch Me the Star, Lamb.

368
00:13:28,340 --> 00:13:29,942
Don't chase the stars, be a star yourself.

369
00:13:30,009 --> 00:13:31,944
That was moving.

370
00:13:32,211 --> 00:13:33,979
HE WASN'T EVEN PAYING ATTENTION…

371
00:13:34,046 --> 00:13:36,348
Sung-jun, what do you do to stay calm?

372
00:13:36,415 --> 00:13:38,617
Of course. When times are tough,

373
00:13:38,684 --> 00:13:40,186
I listen to a song

374
00:13:40,252 --> 00:13:41,987
called "Lion Heart."

375
00:13:42,054 --> 00:13:43,389
Everything he says sounds like a lie.

376
00:13:43,455 --> 00:13:45,291
-I'm serious.
-It just sounds like a lie.

377
00:13:45,357 --> 00:13:47,493
Can you sing a phrase
to help you stay strong?

378
00:13:47,560 --> 00:13:48,761
It's a bit too high.

379
00:13:48,828 --> 00:13:50,796
His credibility just dropped.

380
00:13:50,863 --> 00:13:53,165
-What? Why?
-Right? Isn't that so?

381
00:13:53,232 --> 00:13:54,600
-You felt it, right?
-Yes.

382
00:13:54,667 --> 00:13:56,268
He did it like it was scripted.

383
00:13:56,335 --> 00:13:58,504
-Why?
-She's now suspicious of Sung-jun.

384
00:13:58,571 --> 00:14:02,875
So Sooyoung gets lots of energy
from the song "Rule of the Princess."

385
00:14:02,942 --> 00:14:05,010
Now, I wonder what she has in her fridge.

386
00:14:05,077 --> 00:14:06,312
We're getting curious.

387
00:14:06,378 --> 00:14:07,580
Do you use it alone?

388
00:14:07,646 --> 00:14:08,714
-Yes.
-I see.

389
00:14:08,781 --> 00:14:10,449
It's been about seven years

390
00:14:10,516 --> 00:14:13,219
-that I've lived alone.
-Seven years?

391
00:14:13,285 --> 00:14:15,588
Let's find out what she has.

392
00:14:15,654 --> 00:14:18,023
-We present Sooyoung's fridge!
-Fridge!

393
00:14:18,090 --> 00:14:19,024
WOOHOO

394
00:14:20,392 --> 00:14:22,027
She doesn't have a lot.

395
00:14:22,094 --> 00:14:24,029
-Emergency.
-It's a bit…

396
00:14:24,096 --> 00:14:27,333
Quite a lot of empty space.

397
00:14:27,399 --> 00:14:28,834
She's been busy filming.

398
00:14:28,901 --> 00:14:30,369
Because I live alone,

399
00:14:30,436 --> 00:14:34,406
I often find myself throwing food out
after it expires.

400
00:14:34,473 --> 00:14:36,275
-It happens when living alone.
-It's not easy.

401
00:14:36,342 --> 00:14:38,477
The top shelf has side dishes.

402
00:14:38,544 --> 00:14:40,713
There are lots of basic side dishes.

403
00:14:40,779 --> 00:14:42,548
They might be spoiled.

404
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:46,318
-It's been there for a while.
-Is that so?

405
00:14:46,385 --> 00:14:47,219
SNIFF

406
00:14:47,286 --> 00:14:50,122
-This one is a goner.
-It's been a while.

407
00:14:50,189 --> 00:14:51,523
OH BOY

408
00:14:51,590 --> 00:14:53,292
-Wait a second.
-It smells sour.

409
00:14:53,359 --> 00:14:54,894
-Really?
-Is that kimchi?

410
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:57,196
-It's meat, but it's…
-The meat smells sour?

411
00:14:57,263 --> 00:14:58,130
The meat smells sour.

412
00:14:58,197 --> 00:14:59,698
-Oh, it's expired.
-Right?

413
00:14:59,765 --> 00:15:01,267
It smells that sour?

414
00:15:01,333 --> 00:15:03,002
I thought it was <i>mukeunji.</i>

415
00:15:03,068 --> 00:15:04,436
It's delicious after a toss in a pan.

416
00:15:04,503 --> 00:15:05,537
We should throw it out.

417
00:15:05,604 --> 00:15:06,705
No, please don't.

418
00:15:06,772 --> 00:15:08,374
I'll check and eat it if I can.

419
00:15:08,741 --> 00:15:10,676
WHAT?

420
00:15:12,211 --> 00:15:13,612
It'll be fine once it's warm.

421
00:15:13,679 --> 00:15:15,414
No, you can't do that.

422
00:15:15,481 --> 00:15:17,449
IT'S NOT OKAY…

423
00:15:17,516 --> 00:15:18,350
She's different.

424
00:15:18,417 --> 00:15:19,852
But it's not moldy.

425
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:22,087
-No way.
-It could be moldy somewhere.

426
00:15:22,154 --> 00:15:24,523
-I'll eat it instead.
-By the time it smells sour…

427
00:15:25,724 --> 00:15:26,926
I'll eat it.

428
00:15:26,992 --> 00:15:28,894
-Hey.
-Sung-jun, what?

429
00:15:28,961 --> 00:15:30,629
-You can't.
-I'll eat it for lunch.

430
00:15:30,696 --> 00:15:31,764
You can't.

431
00:15:31,830 --> 00:15:33,699
-I'll leave it out here.
-No way.

432
00:15:34,199 --> 00:15:35,401
THIS IS FOR SUNG-JUN

433
00:15:35,467 --> 00:15:37,503
-It looks good.
-I'm worried about the next one.

434
00:15:37,569 --> 00:15:39,238
What's this?

435
00:15:39,805 --> 00:15:41,006
-Bean sprouts.
-Bean sprouts.

436
00:15:41,073 --> 00:15:43,108
AUTOMATICALLY SMELLS IT FIRST…

437
00:15:43,175 --> 00:15:45,144
It's a little unwell.

438
00:15:45,210 --> 00:15:46,812
It's unwell.

439
00:15:46,879 --> 00:15:48,447
It hasn't gone completely bad yet.

440
00:15:48,514 --> 00:15:50,683
Can you smell things fine?
Do you have a sinus infection?

441
00:15:50,749 --> 00:15:53,619
I think I lost my sense of smell
after the COVID-19 pandemic.

442
00:15:54,787 --> 00:15:58,490
IN HER PRINCESS SPIRIT,
SHE'LL PLAY ALONG WITH EVERYTHING♥

443
00:15:58,891 --> 00:16:01,060
Here's a tip from the production crew.

444
00:16:01,126 --> 00:16:04,596
Sooyoung had once gone
to the emergency room while eating.

445
00:16:04,663 --> 00:16:06,565
-After eating that?
-Did your stomach hurt?

446
00:16:06,632 --> 00:16:09,201
Once I get a taste of something delicious,

447
00:16:09,268 --> 00:16:11,136
I continue to eat and eat.

448
00:16:11,203 --> 00:16:12,538
I like

449
00:16:12,604 --> 00:16:15,441
those cold kimchi noodles they have
at barbecue places for wrap parties.

450
00:16:15,507 --> 00:16:18,043
The kind that's served on the side.

451
00:16:18,110 --> 00:16:19,778
I was eating that,

452
00:16:19,845 --> 00:16:21,680
and then I suddenly had a headache.

453
00:16:21,747 --> 00:16:24,116
It felt like I had food up to my neck

454
00:16:24,183 --> 00:16:27,052
and had cut off circulation to my head.

455
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:29,922
-You ate that much?
-Was it indigestion?

456
00:16:29,989 --> 00:16:32,524
So I got my stomach pumped
at the emergency room.

457
00:16:33,025 --> 00:16:34,960
You just force yourself to keep eating?

458
00:16:35,027 --> 00:16:36,595
I'm more captivated by the flavor

459
00:16:36,662 --> 00:16:37,963
-than the fullness.
-I know that.

460
00:16:38,030 --> 00:16:40,799
-I know what she means.
-Because it's that good?

461
00:16:40,866 --> 00:16:42,935
Nam-no, can you understand this situation?

462
00:16:43,002 --> 00:16:44,169
Have you had indigestion?

463
00:16:44,236 --> 00:16:45,704
I suffer from it often.

464
00:16:45,771 --> 00:16:46,905
You often suffer from it?

465
00:16:46,972 --> 00:16:48,507
I've been to the emergency room too.

466
00:16:48,574 --> 00:16:49,808
-What?
-For eating too much?

467
00:16:49,875 --> 00:16:50,943
I was in my mid-twenties,

468
00:16:51,010 --> 00:16:53,512
and I had tried top-grade Korean beef
for the first time.

469
00:16:54,079 --> 00:16:56,648
It was so good that it made my head spin.

470
00:16:56,715 --> 00:16:59,752
-Made his head spin?
-I alone probably had

471
00:16:59,818 --> 00:17:01,653
about 1.1 kg of beef
along with <i>somaek,</i> soju and beer.

472
00:17:01,720 --> 00:17:03,555
-My head is spinning now.
-Over a kilogram?

473
00:17:03,622 --> 00:17:05,424
-About eight portions then.
-It was my first time.

474
00:17:05,491 --> 00:17:07,626
When you're too full,
oxygen level drops in your head.

475
00:17:07,693 --> 00:17:09,328
-He's right.
-Oxygen?

476
00:17:09,395 --> 00:17:10,696
They had the same symptoms,

477
00:17:10,763 --> 00:17:12,798
but they ended up in two different shapes.

478
00:17:12,865 --> 00:17:14,566
THE MYSTERIES OF THE HUMAN BODY

479
00:17:14,633 --> 00:17:15,467
So you enjoy eating?

480
00:17:15,534 --> 00:17:17,936
I love to eat. I love delicious things.

481
00:17:18,003 --> 00:17:20,072
I see cheese on the next shelf.

482
00:17:20,139 --> 00:17:22,841
-She has lots of cheese.
-There's burrata.

483
00:17:22,908 --> 00:17:24,076
You must like cheese.

484
00:17:24,143 --> 00:17:25,711
I like to grind…

485
00:17:25,778 --> 00:17:28,714
-And sprinkle it?
-…and sprinkle it on pasta as a kick.

486
00:17:28,781 --> 00:17:30,516
I see. Used as a kick.

487
00:17:30,582 --> 00:17:32,518
Are these anchovies?

488
00:17:32,584 --> 00:17:34,186
-They are.
-Anchovies, right?

489
00:17:34,253 --> 00:17:35,654
I love anchovy pasta.

490
00:17:35,721 --> 00:17:37,723
-That sounds good.
-I wanted to get it,

491
00:17:37,790 --> 00:17:40,292
so I bought one
during my visit to America,

492
00:17:40,359 --> 00:17:42,394
but I haven't used it yet.

493
00:17:42,461 --> 00:17:44,329
-There they are.
-She has them.

494
00:17:44,396 --> 00:17:45,664
-You have pasta too.
-Yes.

495
00:17:45,731 --> 00:17:46,999
-She has pasta.
-Do you make it?

496
00:17:47,733 --> 00:17:49,334
-Yes, at times.
-I'll make anchovy pasta.

497
00:17:49,401 --> 00:17:51,870
-When I crave pasta…
-That's mine.

498
00:17:51,937 --> 00:17:54,973
…but don't want to get it delivered,
I make pasta for myself.

499
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:56,975
So she does cook at home.

500
00:17:57,042 --> 00:17:58,510
I try to maximize…

501
00:17:58,577 --> 00:18:01,780
I mean, minimize the number of tools I use
whenever I cook.

502
00:18:01,847 --> 00:18:03,982
Cleaning up is a hassle.

503
00:18:04,049 --> 00:18:05,584
It's such a hassle.

504
00:18:05,651 --> 00:18:06,485
I should cook for her.

505
00:18:06,552 --> 00:18:08,120
You're the type that can't be bothered.

506
00:18:08,187 --> 00:18:09,888
Yes, I'm like that.

507
00:18:09,955 --> 00:18:12,724
I even wonder
if using the cutting board is necessary.

508
00:18:12,791 --> 00:18:14,293
I sit and wonder…

509
00:18:14,359 --> 00:18:16,261
-Scissors?
-…if I should use it.

510
00:18:16,328 --> 00:18:18,464
I'd end up resorting to scissors,

511
00:18:18,530 --> 00:18:20,499
and if my half-hearted attempt works,

512
00:18:20,566 --> 00:18:22,601
I tell myself,
"I'm glad I didn't use the board."

513
00:18:22,668 --> 00:18:26,105
Or you can get pre-prepped vegetables.

514
00:18:26,171 --> 00:18:29,274
-But I don't like to use those.
-Not those?

515
00:18:29,341 --> 00:18:33,078
I believe you must cut the ingredients
on the spot as you cook.

516
00:18:33,145 --> 00:18:36,048
-I can connect.
-Right?

517
00:18:36,115 --> 00:18:37,649
Right? The pre-cut ones…

518
00:18:37,716 --> 00:18:40,052
-Those are lifeless.
-Yes, they're lifeless.

519
00:18:40,119 --> 00:18:41,854
They're lifeless?

520
00:18:41,920 --> 00:18:43,388
"INGREDIENTS MUST HAVE LIFE"
BY MS. CHOI

521
00:18:43,455 --> 00:18:44,423
Is your food good?

522
00:18:44,490 --> 00:18:45,757
I think I make

523
00:18:46,258 --> 00:18:47,759
pretty good stuff.

524
00:18:47,826 --> 00:18:49,328
She's confident.

525
00:18:49,394 --> 00:18:50,963
We need an objective answer.

526
00:18:51,029 --> 00:18:52,331
I never even have to check while cooking.

527
00:18:52,397 --> 00:18:55,901
I have a good sense
of figuring out when it's perfect.

528
00:18:55,968 --> 00:18:59,438
-I believe cooking is all about timing.
-Timing.

529
00:18:59,505 --> 00:19:02,374
Those who fail at cooking

530
00:19:02,441 --> 00:19:05,644
probably fail because of their impatience.

531
00:19:05,711 --> 00:19:07,212
Keep staring

532
00:19:07,279 --> 00:19:09,314
and lock into a power struggle
with your food.

533
00:19:09,381 --> 00:19:11,250
"Not yet."

534
00:19:11,316 --> 00:19:13,118
And then! I finish it.

535
00:19:13,185 --> 00:19:14,453
-Right.
-The timing.

536
00:19:14,520 --> 00:19:16,221
I'm also an expert at making porridge.

537
00:19:16,288 --> 00:19:17,489
-Porridge?
-Porridge?

538
00:19:17,556 --> 00:19:18,757
Porridge.

539
00:19:18,824 --> 00:19:21,493
After we're done with shabu-shabu,
we always finish the meal

540
00:19:21,560 --> 00:19:23,195
-with porridge, right?
-Yes, you're right.

541
00:19:23,262 --> 00:19:26,832
-That's porridge.
-When I eat shabu-shabu with my staff,

542
00:19:26,899 --> 00:19:28,400
I'm always in charge
of making the porridge,

543
00:19:28,467 --> 00:19:30,002
and it's to die for.

544
00:19:30,068 --> 00:19:31,170
PORRIDGE PRIDE

545
00:19:31,236 --> 00:19:34,273
-It sounds good.
-Waiting is key when making porridge.

546
00:19:34,339 --> 00:19:36,775
The timing for adding the egg
is very important.

547
00:19:36,842 --> 00:19:38,443
-It's important.
-That moment

548
00:19:38,510 --> 00:19:40,112
when you mix the egg in.

549
00:19:40,179 --> 00:19:41,713
-Then work with the residual heat.
-Exactly!

550
00:19:41,780 --> 00:19:43,982
-You know exactly what's up.
-Yes.

551
00:19:44,049 --> 00:19:45,884
-As it simmers.
-Lastly, a drop of sesame oil.

552
00:19:45,951 --> 00:19:47,186
At the very end.

553
00:19:47,252 --> 00:19:48,787
Too early, and you lose the aroma.

554
00:19:48,854 --> 00:19:49,922
We won't allow that.

555
00:19:49,988 --> 00:19:51,657
-Right at the end.
-You know what's up.

556
00:19:51,723 --> 00:19:53,225
You just can't be bothered,

557
00:19:53,292 --> 00:19:55,761
-but when you actually do it…
-I do it right.

558
00:19:55,827 --> 00:19:56,995
What's this?

559
00:19:57,062 --> 00:19:59,798
-Freshwater snails.
-Freshwater snails?

560
00:19:59,865 --> 00:20:01,066
-Salmon.
-Salmon?

561
00:20:01,133 --> 00:20:02,501
-Duck.
-<i>Jamón.</i>

562
00:20:02,568 --> 00:20:03,802
<i>-Jamón.</i>
-Right.

563
00:20:03,869 --> 00:20:06,405
I consider protein very important,

564
00:20:06,471 --> 00:20:07,906
so even when I don't want to cook,

565
00:20:07,973 --> 00:20:10,609
I still want to have some protein.

566
00:20:10,676 --> 00:20:14,746
When I have time, I'd make
a huge batch of freshwater snail <i>doenjang</i>

567
00:20:14,813 --> 00:20:19,351
and eat veggie and rice wraps
with that as the sauce.

568
00:20:19,418 --> 00:20:20,886
I eat salmon and <i>jamón</i>

569
00:20:20,953 --> 00:20:22,788
to make American-style breakfast,

570
00:20:22,854 --> 00:20:26,592
served with some bread and eggs.

571
00:20:27,292 --> 00:20:28,794
This is sweet jelly,

572
00:20:28,860 --> 00:20:30,229
and there's a princess right here.

573
00:20:30,295 --> 00:20:33,632
-Gongju, just like "<i>gongju</i>" for princess.
-Yes.

574
00:20:33,699 --> 00:20:36,635
-Red bean jelly with chestnuts. <i>Yanggaeng</i>.
-"Rule of the Princess."

575
00:20:36,702 --> 00:20:39,905
I see some alcohol on this side.

576
00:20:39,972 --> 00:20:41,640
I see your name on this bottle.

577
00:20:41,707 --> 00:20:44,142
One of my fans engraved it with my name

578
00:20:44,209 --> 00:20:45,978
-and gave it to me…
-A rosé?

579
00:20:46,044 --> 00:20:47,346
-…for my birthday.
-That's a thing?

580
00:20:47,412 --> 00:20:50,382
-February 10th, 1990. Is that right?
-You're right.

581
00:20:50,449 --> 00:20:51,950
That's when you got it?

582
00:20:52,017 --> 00:20:54,319
-No.
-No, that's just my birthday.

583
00:20:56,822 --> 00:20:59,258
-It's her birthday.
-Her birthday.

584
00:20:59,324 --> 00:21:01,226
-Can you drink a bottle alone?
-Yes.

585
00:21:01,293 --> 00:21:02,594
-I can do that.
-A bottle of wine.

586
00:21:02,661 --> 00:21:04,596
How much alcohol can you take, Jung-hwa?

587
00:21:05,397 --> 00:21:07,199
I'm just like her.

588
00:21:07,266 --> 00:21:09,735
She can take much more alcohol than I can.

589
00:21:09,801 --> 00:21:12,504
-We're about the same.
-Excuse me.

590
00:21:12,571 --> 00:21:14,106
Are you talking about the magnum size?

591
00:21:14,172 --> 00:21:15,607
A BOTTLE OF THIS?

592
00:21:17,209 --> 00:21:19,044
-Just a regular bottle.
-One.

593
00:21:19,111 --> 00:21:22,281
A bottle of wine,
a bottle of whiskey, and a bottle of soju.

594
00:21:22,347 --> 00:21:25,550
-A bottle of different kinds?
-One bottle each.

595
00:21:27,819 --> 00:21:31,189
What's Jung-hwa like
after she drinks a little?

596
00:21:31,256 --> 00:21:33,725
She can be really adorable.

597
00:21:33,792 --> 00:21:36,828
-I begin to laugh a lot.
-Yes, she does that.

598
00:21:36,895 --> 00:21:38,196
Sooyoung dances.

599
00:21:38,263 --> 00:21:39,231
-You do?
-Yes.

600
00:21:39,298 --> 00:21:40,999
Do you do the flips?

601
00:21:41,066 --> 00:21:42,601
This hair thing. The flip.

602
00:21:42,668 --> 00:21:45,570
I wanted to be cute when I was with her.

603
00:21:45,637 --> 00:21:47,439
A CUTE JUNIOR ACTOR♥

604
00:21:47,506 --> 00:21:49,574
What's in here?

605
00:21:49,641 --> 00:21:51,510
-Bread.
-Bread.

606
00:21:51,576 --> 00:21:52,911
-Is that focaccia?
-That is

607
00:21:52,978 --> 00:21:54,946
my favorite, called slab bread.

608
00:21:55,013 --> 00:21:56,148
That's huge.

609
00:21:56,214 --> 00:21:58,083
It's big enough to be used as a cushion.

610
00:21:58,150 --> 00:21:59,484
Or a pillow.

611
00:21:59,551 --> 00:22:01,253
I also love figs,

612
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:04,690
so I like to eat them
with pistachio spread,

613
00:22:04,756 --> 00:22:08,794
-by turning them into a sandwich.
-So you make a sandwich.

614
00:22:08,860 --> 00:22:11,096
-Chicken.
-You have some chicken here.

615
00:22:11,163 --> 00:22:14,333
I really like spicy braised chicken.

616
00:22:14,399 --> 00:22:16,101
That's not an easy dish to make.

617
00:22:16,168 --> 00:22:17,536
I can even make it with my feet.

618
00:22:17,803 --> 00:22:21,073
DROP THE MIC

619
00:22:21,139 --> 00:22:23,575
I see. She dribbles the ingredients.

620
00:22:23,642 --> 00:22:25,644
Now, non-perishable ingredients.

621
00:22:25,711 --> 00:22:28,513
Oh, you must drink tea at home.

622
00:22:28,580 --> 00:22:31,083
I was deeply into tea ceremonies
for a while.

623
00:22:31,149 --> 00:22:32,484
She was into tea ceremonies?

624
00:22:32,551 --> 00:22:34,219
But after just two times, I just…

625
00:22:34,286 --> 00:22:35,687
-Couldn't be bothered?
-…couldn't be bothered.

626
00:22:35,954 --> 00:22:38,390
HER CHRONIC LAZINESS KICKED IN

627
00:22:38,990 --> 00:22:40,692
-I couldn't do it.
-You end up using a mug.

628
00:22:40,759 --> 00:22:42,627
-You have to throw out the dregs.
-I get it.

629
00:22:42,694 --> 00:22:43,895
I picked it up

630
00:22:43,962 --> 00:22:47,699
because the time I waited
for the tea to brew made me…

631
00:22:47,766 --> 00:22:51,169
-It's calming.
-Yes, it was quite calming.

632
00:22:51,236 --> 00:22:53,472
Then one day,

633
00:22:53,538 --> 00:22:57,709
I realized I could be more patient
even without brewing the tea.

634
00:22:57,776 --> 00:23:00,045
I began to wonder
if this action was necessary

635
00:23:00,112 --> 00:23:02,981
for me to build more patience,

636
00:23:03,048 --> 00:23:05,150
so I did some self-reflection,

637
00:23:05,217 --> 00:23:08,120
and switched all my teas to tea bags.

638
00:23:08,353 --> 00:23:09,921
CONVENIENCE IS THE BEST

639
00:23:09,988 --> 00:23:11,656
-It's convenient.
-That's true.

640
00:23:11,723 --> 00:23:13,091
Tea bags are delicious.

641
00:23:13,158 --> 00:23:15,560
That's it for Sooyoung's fridge!

642
00:23:17,596 --> 00:23:20,999
I wonder what her orders might be.

643
00:23:21,066 --> 00:23:23,735
Let's find out what they are.

644
00:23:23,802 --> 00:23:25,103
Show us.

645
00:23:25,670 --> 00:23:28,373
-First order. Rule of the Princess's Dish.
-Rule of the Princess's Dish.

646
00:23:28,573 --> 00:23:29,608
LIKE THE SONG SHE MENTIONED

647
00:23:29,674 --> 00:23:30,675
Make her a princess?

648
00:23:30,742 --> 00:23:33,178
I've recently been

649
00:23:33,245 --> 00:23:36,548
too busy to eat right.

650
00:23:36,615 --> 00:23:40,218
All I eat is simples things
like salad or <i>gimbap,</i>

651
00:23:40,285 --> 00:23:43,422
so I've been craving
something very fancy and grand.

652
00:23:43,655 --> 00:23:45,056
I GET IT

653
00:23:45,123 --> 00:23:47,626
So I want something very fancy
that can recharge my energy

654
00:23:47,692 --> 00:23:48,894
as a princess.

655
00:23:49,861 --> 00:23:51,963
-A fancy dish.
-Like a big treat.

656
00:23:52,030 --> 00:23:54,833
But the thing is, my ingredients

657
00:23:54,900 --> 00:23:56,802
are a bit too humble.

658
00:23:56,868 --> 00:24:00,539
Our chef will
dress them up like a princess.

659
00:24:00,605 --> 00:24:03,608
-Yes, of course.
-She needs that princess energy.

660
00:24:03,675 --> 00:24:06,178
Here's the second order.

661
00:24:06,244 --> 00:24:08,413
Don't Skip Meals
Because You Can't Be Bothered.

662
00:24:09,448 --> 00:24:11,683
You seemed to be quite lazy.

663
00:24:11,750 --> 00:24:14,085
I often can't be bothered,

664
00:24:14,152 --> 00:24:18,190
so I want to eat something
that's easy and breezy to make

665
00:24:18,256 --> 00:24:19,891
but also very delicious.

666
00:24:21,393 --> 00:24:22,327
That's what I want.

667
00:24:22,394 --> 00:24:25,163
Now, take a look at the orders
and jump in, chefs.

668
00:24:25,230 --> 00:24:28,200
There is someone
who had been dying to have her here,

669
00:24:28,266 --> 00:24:31,470
-Sooyoung's Hubby.
-We should have him choose first.

670
00:24:31,536 --> 00:24:33,338
I'm going to pick something, but…

671
00:24:33,405 --> 00:24:34,272
GETS UP

672
00:24:34,339 --> 00:24:35,740
What's that?

673
00:24:35,807 --> 00:24:37,275
The princess seemed chilly.

674
00:24:37,342 --> 00:24:39,010
Wait, what the heck?

675
00:24:39,377 --> 00:24:41,012
A BLANKET FOR PRINCESS SOOYOUNG

676
00:24:41,079 --> 00:24:42,147
Wait, what the heck?

677
00:24:42,214 --> 00:24:44,583
-Yes, it's a bit chilly.
-Isn't it cold?

678
00:24:45,183 --> 00:24:46,718
THE PRINCESS WHO FEELS COLD

679
00:24:47,285 --> 00:24:49,754
AND A MAN WHO NOTICED

680
00:24:49,821 --> 00:24:51,456
I was keeping an eye on her,
and she seemed cold.

681
00:24:51,690 --> 00:24:53,091
MOVED

682
00:24:53,425 --> 00:24:55,293
WHAT DID I JUST WITNESS?

683
00:24:55,360 --> 00:24:56,862
When I said I was cold, you just said…

684
00:24:56,928 --> 00:24:58,196
-You did?
-…"Why are you cold?"

685
00:24:59,464 --> 00:25:00,732
Dang it.

686
00:25:00,799 --> 00:25:02,834
Jung-hwa also seems a bit chilly.

687
00:25:03,101 --> 00:25:04,736
LOL

688
00:25:04,803 --> 00:25:06,471
Please don't.

689
00:25:06,538 --> 00:25:08,440
-Look at her. She's also cold.
-Sit down.

690
00:25:08,507 --> 00:25:10,375
-No?
-She's fine.

691
00:25:10,442 --> 00:25:12,611
-What are you doing?
-She seemed chilly.

692
00:25:12,677 --> 00:25:14,012
This won't be enough.

693
00:25:14,079 --> 00:25:17,048
-Sung-jun, you get the first pick.
-Yes, I should go first.

694
00:25:17,115 --> 00:25:18,049
Of course, I'll go

695
00:25:18,116 --> 00:25:20,752
-with Rule of the Princess's Dish.
-Rule of the Princess's Dish.

696
00:25:20,819 --> 00:25:22,587
I've been waiting for this day.

697
00:25:22,654 --> 00:25:26,358
Then who's going to challenge
Sung-jun, aka Sooyoung's Hubby?

698
00:25:26,691 --> 00:25:28,193
GLANCES

699
00:25:28,260 --> 00:25:29,094
RAISING HAND

700
00:25:29,327 --> 00:25:30,495
WHAT?

701
00:25:30,562 --> 00:25:33,832
This princess deserved to stand
in the center a long time ago.

702
00:25:33,899 --> 00:25:35,200
I'll give her what she deserves.

703
00:25:35,433 --> 00:25:38,069
HYUN-SUK PICKS RULE OF THE PRINCESS'S DISH

704
00:25:38,136 --> 00:25:41,006
He can be Sooyoung's Unc,
like an older guy fan.

705
00:25:41,072 --> 00:25:43,074
Hyun-suk joins the first round.

706
00:25:43,141 --> 00:25:44,609
That's interesting.

707
00:25:44,676 --> 00:25:46,511
Don't Skip Meals
Because You Can't Be Bothered.

708
00:25:46,578 --> 00:25:48,647
-I'll join.
-Hey.

709
00:25:48,713 --> 00:25:50,849
-Nam-no?
-Yes, the can't-be-bothered round.

710
00:25:50,916 --> 00:25:53,151
But he can always be bothered for food.

711
00:25:53,218 --> 00:25:56,087
I'm going to use
a minimal amount of cooking

712
00:25:56,154 --> 00:25:57,656
to maximize the flavors.

713
00:25:57,722 --> 00:25:59,591
-He's good at that.
-He is.

714
00:25:59,658 --> 00:26:01,092
You actually understood the order.

715
00:26:01,159 --> 00:26:03,628
Yes, I actually managed
to figure it out today.

716
00:26:03,695 --> 00:26:05,196
Something you can do with your feet.

717
00:26:05,263 --> 00:26:06,331
Do it with your feet.

718
00:26:06,398 --> 00:26:07,832
I've never cooked with my feet.

719
00:26:08,066 --> 00:26:10,602
SHE DOESN'T MEAN IT LITERALLY…

720
00:26:10,669 --> 00:26:12,170
Who wants to face Nam-no?

721
00:26:12,237 --> 00:26:13,438
Or join it for the order.

722
00:26:13,505 --> 00:26:14,806
I'll go.

723
00:26:14,873 --> 00:26:17,042
EUN-YEONG PICKS DON'T SKIP MEALS
BECAUSE YOU CAN'T BE BOTHERED

724
00:26:17,108 --> 00:26:19,277
I also have that lazy side,

725
00:26:19,344 --> 00:26:20,645
You do.

726
00:26:20,712 --> 00:26:22,781
…and it's been a while
since I've won a star.

727
00:26:22,847 --> 00:26:27,152
So I want to take down Chef Nam-no,
our weakest contestant,

728
00:26:27,218 --> 00:26:28,587
-and change the course.
-"Weakest"?

729
00:26:28,653 --> 00:26:29,988
That was harsh.

730
00:26:30,055 --> 00:26:32,257
How did he end up becoming the weakest?

731
00:26:32,324 --> 00:26:34,793
That's Nam-no versus Eun-yeong then.

732
00:26:34,859 --> 00:26:37,095
Let us begin Rule of the Princess's Dish,

733
00:26:37,162 --> 00:26:40,699
a round between Hyun-suk and Sung-jun!

734
00:26:40,765 --> 00:26:42,601
I've got chills. I'm excited.

735
00:26:42,667 --> 00:26:43,535
This is great.

736
00:26:43,602 --> 00:26:46,237
-I'm so excited.
-All right.

737
00:26:46,304 --> 00:26:50,642
<i>This is the first cook-off</i>
<i>with Sooyoung's ingredients.</i>

738
00:26:50,709 --> 00:26:54,946
Sooyoung's Hubby for 20 years,
Chef Kwon Sung-jun,

739
00:26:55,013 --> 00:26:57,048
versus the guy
who's willing to be her grandpa,

740
00:26:57,115 --> 00:26:59,884
Chef Choi Hyun-suk.

741
00:26:59,951 --> 00:27:02,153
<i>They played as a team</i>
<i>in the previous episode.</i>

742
00:27:02,220 --> 00:27:04,589
After that team round,
Hyun-suk said he aged by a decade

743
00:27:04,656 --> 00:27:05,890
after cooking with Sung-jun.

744
00:27:05,957 --> 00:27:07,792
-Did you say this?
-Why?

745
00:27:07,859 --> 00:27:09,327
It's much easier

746
00:27:09,394 --> 00:27:11,129
to have Sung-jun as my opponent

747
00:27:11,196 --> 00:27:14,332
than to work with him in a team.

748
00:27:14,599 --> 00:27:16,635
IT MUST'VE BEEN QUITE A JOURNEY…

749
00:27:16,701 --> 00:27:17,802
For a team round,

750
00:27:17,869 --> 00:27:20,905
we're supposed to work together
and make the dishes together.

751
00:27:20,972 --> 00:27:22,440
But when we were discussing recipes,

752
00:27:22,507 --> 00:27:23,775
he wasn't looking for teamwork.

753
00:27:23,842 --> 00:27:26,211
He said, "You're going to do that?
I'll do this then."

754
00:27:26,444 --> 00:27:27,512
EACH ON THEIR OWN

755
00:27:27,579 --> 00:27:28,480
He refuses to mix.

756
00:27:28,546 --> 00:27:31,516
I don't always have to be
the one to score the goal.

757
00:27:31,583 --> 00:27:32,984
I just want the team to win.

758
00:27:33,051 --> 00:27:36,354
But this guy needs to score
the most decisive goal himself.

759
00:27:37,055 --> 00:27:39,424
It has to go through him.

760
00:27:39,491 --> 00:27:41,459
What's your take on this account?

761
00:27:41,526 --> 00:27:43,194
I completely agree.

762
00:27:43,261 --> 00:27:45,330
-You do?
-Yes.

763
00:27:45,397 --> 00:27:47,032
This cook-off today

764
00:27:47,098 --> 00:27:49,434
-must have a special meaning for you.
-It does.

765
00:27:49,501 --> 00:27:51,903
The one you've always waited for,

766
00:27:51,970 --> 00:27:55,373
-Sooyoung, is finally here.
-"Sooyoung's Hubby."

767
00:27:55,440 --> 00:27:58,843
-I didn't want to bring up this data, but…
-What is it?

768
00:27:58,910 --> 00:28:00,679
He's jinxed at the moment.

769
00:28:00,745 --> 00:28:02,280
-Don't bring it up.
-I know.

770
00:28:02,347 --> 00:28:05,717
Everyone and their mother knows this.

771
00:28:05,784 --> 00:28:08,620
Every time a K-pop idol star
brings their fridge to the studio…

772
00:28:08,687 --> 00:28:10,855
He lost all ten rounds.

773
00:28:10,922 --> 00:28:12,524
He hasn't won once.

774
00:28:12,590 --> 00:28:14,092
-He's jinxed.
-How does this happen?

775
00:28:14,159 --> 00:28:16,127
-It's that bad?
-Here's the thing.

776
00:28:16,194 --> 00:28:20,131
Before receiving a star
from the first bias of my life, Sooyoung,

777
00:28:20,198 --> 00:28:21,900
I couldn't take it from anyone else.

778
00:28:21,966 --> 00:28:23,535
SUSPICIOUS

779
00:28:23,601 --> 00:28:25,804
But you tried hard to win.

780
00:28:25,870 --> 00:28:27,806
To a man, his first love will always be

781
00:28:27,872 --> 00:28:29,507
unforgettable.

782
00:28:29,574 --> 00:28:32,010
SHRIEK!

783
00:28:32,077 --> 00:28:33,578
Is there a cockroach?

784
00:28:33,645 --> 00:28:36,514
-I'll throw these at him. I will.
-What happened?

785
00:28:36,581 --> 00:28:37,882
You're really desperate.

786
00:28:37,949 --> 00:28:39,718
Her star has a whole new meaning.

787
00:28:40,652 --> 00:28:42,487
CHEF HYUN-SUK'S INGREDIENTS:
GRAVLAX, SLICED CHEESE, BURRATA

788
00:28:42,554 --> 00:28:44,723
YUJA PEPPER PASTE, ZUCCHINI, SHRIMP,
CURRY POWDER, CHAMPAGNE, AND MORE

789
00:28:44,789 --> 00:28:47,959
First up, Chef Hyun-suk.
What are you making?

790
00:28:48,026 --> 00:28:51,129
The name of my dish is Choipunzel.

791
00:28:51,196 --> 00:28:53,031
-Choipunzel.
-Choipunzel?

792
00:28:53,098 --> 00:28:55,133
Rapunzel is my favorite princess.

793
00:28:55,200 --> 00:28:59,037
SOOYOUNG'S BIAS, RAPUNZEL

794
00:28:59,104 --> 00:29:00,872
-Emergency.
-You did it again, Hyun-suk.

795
00:29:00,939 --> 00:29:04,709
You express your beauty and charm

796
00:29:04,776 --> 00:29:08,079
using your hair, right?

797
00:29:08,146 --> 00:29:10,248
There's a thin kind of pasta in Italy

798
00:29:10,315 --> 00:29:12,283
called angel hair.

799
00:29:12,350 --> 00:29:15,620
So I'll make pasta today
with princess hair,

800
00:29:15,687 --> 00:29:17,889
along with a pretty appetizer

801
00:29:17,956 --> 00:29:19,791
for the princess's meal.

802
00:29:19,858 --> 00:29:21,826
-My gosh. I'm so excited.
-European royalty

803
00:29:21,893 --> 00:29:25,096
would travel around with private chefs

804
00:29:25,163 --> 00:29:28,466
and use different ingredients
as they moved to different countries.

805
00:29:28,533 --> 00:29:30,835
I'll be your private chef,

806
00:29:30,902 --> 00:29:32,437
follow you around the world,

807
00:29:32,504 --> 00:29:35,039
and make your food with local ingredients.

808
00:29:35,540 --> 00:29:37,375
LEAVE IT TO ME, PRINCESS

809
00:29:37,675 --> 00:29:40,645
VERY PLEASED♥

810
00:29:40,712 --> 00:29:41,713
-How cool.
-Not angel hair.

811
00:29:41,780 --> 00:29:43,982
Are you going to make
this princess hair yourself?

812
00:29:44,048 --> 00:29:46,184
-I'll do it myself.
-Fresh pasta?

813
00:29:46,251 --> 00:29:48,219
Because store-bought pasta

814
00:29:48,286 --> 00:29:51,422
cannot embody Sooyoung's beautiful hair.

815
00:29:51,489 --> 00:29:52,724
So you're making fresh pasta?

816
00:29:52,791 --> 00:29:54,125
Can he make thin noodles?

817
00:29:54,192 --> 00:29:57,228
-Angel hair is really thin.
-It has to be very thin.

818
00:29:57,295 --> 00:29:58,963
I'm not sure if it'll be possible.

819
00:29:59,798 --> 00:30:02,267
CHEF SUNG-JUN'S INGREDIENTS:
ANCHOVY, CAPER, GRAVLAX, JAMÓN

820
00:30:02,333 --> 00:30:05,470
YANGGAENG WITH CHESTNUTS, SEAWEED BUGAK,
PISTACHIO CREAM, BURRATA, AND MORE

821
00:30:05,537 --> 00:30:07,238
Sung-jun must feel anxious.

822
00:30:07,305 --> 00:30:08,673
So what are you making?

823
00:30:09,174 --> 00:30:10,441
The dish I prepared is…

824
00:30:10,508 --> 00:30:12,243
It's called Into Three New Worlds.

825
00:30:12,310 --> 00:30:13,711
Into the New World?

826
00:30:13,778 --> 00:30:15,580
DOESN'T WANT TO MEET THE NEW SUNG-JUN

827
00:30:15,647 --> 00:30:18,116
It's a parody of "Into the New World,"

828
00:30:18,183 --> 00:30:19,517
so it's Into Three New Worlds.

829
00:30:19,584 --> 00:30:21,686
-Three.
-Three.

830
00:30:21,753 --> 00:30:23,288
-Three.
-I prepared

831
00:30:23,354 --> 00:30:25,056
a three-course Italian meal.

832
00:30:25,123 --> 00:30:26,391
You're making three dishes?

833
00:30:26,457 --> 00:30:28,760
I've never made
actual authentic pasta here.

834
00:30:28,827 --> 00:30:31,329
I thought it'd be expected of me.

835
00:30:31,396 --> 00:30:32,864
But even though it's a cliché,

836
00:30:32,931 --> 00:30:36,801
I want to face Hyun-suk head-on
by making a very delicious dish.

837
00:30:36,868 --> 00:30:39,671
-Gosh, I'm so excited.
-The first one is the appetizer.

838
00:30:39,737 --> 00:30:44,409
<i>Pistachio, burrata, and ham</i>
<i>create a great balance.</i>

839
00:30:44,475 --> 00:30:46,845
I'll make them into the shape of a flower.

840
00:30:46,911 --> 00:30:48,980
Next, I'm going to make anchovy pasta.

841
00:30:49,047 --> 00:30:50,949
-She said she liked it.
-You mentioned it earlier.

842
00:30:51,015 --> 00:30:52,851
I'm making anchovy oil pasta,

843
00:30:52,917 --> 00:30:55,386
and topping it with gravlax tartar
to make it even fancier.

844
00:30:55,453 --> 00:30:57,188
And lastly,

845
00:30:57,255 --> 00:30:59,657
I'll use chestnut <i>yanggaeng</i> from Gongju
for the princess, <i>gongju,</i>

846
00:30:59,724 --> 00:31:02,594
-and make panna cotta.
-Panna cotta.

847
00:31:02,660 --> 00:31:04,028
-Panna cotta.
-In 15 minutes?

848
00:31:04,295 --> 00:31:05,530
THREE DISHES FOR PRINCESS SOOYOUNG

849
00:31:05,597 --> 00:31:09,567
You have a favor to ask her
if you end up winning today?

850
00:31:09,634 --> 00:31:12,503
Since my first year
at Eulji Middle School,

851
00:31:12,570 --> 00:31:14,906
I've always dreamed of this one moment.

852
00:31:14,973 --> 00:31:16,341
"Into the New World" with her.

853
00:31:16,407 --> 00:31:17,876
-Does he want to dance?
-With her?

854
00:31:17,942 --> 00:31:18,810
I want to dance with her.

855
00:31:20,545 --> 00:31:22,080
If you put yourself in her shoes,

856
00:31:22,146 --> 00:31:23,281
she may not want to do it.

857
00:31:23,348 --> 00:31:25,516
She might end up
not choosing you intentionally.

858
00:31:25,583 --> 00:31:28,386
-I've dreamed of this for 20 years.
-His dream of 20 years.

859
00:31:28,453 --> 00:31:29,921
If he wins, he wants to dance with you.

860
00:31:29,988 --> 00:31:31,289
I decline.

861
00:31:31,356 --> 00:31:32,323
I decline.

862
00:31:33,791 --> 00:31:35,927
We also don't want to see it.

863
00:31:35,994 --> 00:31:39,364
-You'll have to agree first.
-Yes.

864
00:31:39,430 --> 00:31:41,532
Getting declined
wasn't a part of my dream.

865
00:31:43,301 --> 00:31:45,737
-For now, let's try to win.
-First, I'll win.

866
00:31:45,803 --> 00:31:48,439
-You'll have to win first.
-She might agree to dance with you.

867
00:31:48,506 --> 00:31:50,441
You just have to win.

868
00:31:50,508 --> 00:31:53,878
She's trying to make this fair
for Chef Hyun-suk.

869
00:31:53,945 --> 00:31:57,148
And now, let us begin the round.

870
00:31:57,215 --> 00:31:59,517
-I'm so excited.
-Excellent.

871
00:31:59,584 --> 00:32:02,353
He has waited 20 years for this day.

872
00:32:02,420 --> 00:32:06,190
Sooyoung's Hubby of Eulji Middle School,
Chef Kwon Sung-jun.

873
00:32:06,457 --> 00:32:07,659
FLATTERED AND EMBARRASSED

874
00:32:07,725 --> 00:32:09,861
He claims Sooyoung
is the center of Girls' Generation

875
00:32:09,928 --> 00:32:12,263
and he's the center of <i>Chef & My Fridge.</i>

876
00:32:12,330 --> 00:32:16,534
Here to show the class as the center,
Chef Hyun-suk is up against him.

877
00:32:16,601 --> 00:32:20,004
Which one will become
Princess Sooyoung's private chef?

878
00:32:20,071 --> 00:32:22,607
Let the 15-minute cook-off begin!

879
00:32:24,342 --> 00:32:26,144
A DISH FOR THE PRINCESS

880
00:32:27,045 --> 00:32:29,080
-He starts with pasta.
-Yes.

881
00:32:29,147 --> 00:32:31,649
-Sung-jun uses regular pasta.
-Yes.

882
00:32:31,716 --> 00:32:33,618
Please make her a very fancy meal.

883
00:32:33,685 --> 00:32:36,020
He said he'd make panna cotta,

884
00:32:36,087 --> 00:32:38,256
so I'm curious to see how he'll do that.

885
00:32:38,323 --> 00:32:39,924
He needs something similar to cream.

886
00:32:39,991 --> 00:32:42,226
-There are no ingredients like that.
-She didn't have gelatin, either.

887
00:32:42,293 --> 00:32:43,428
No, she didn't have gelatin.

888
00:32:43,494 --> 00:32:45,196
It won't be easy to make in time.

889
00:32:45,263 --> 00:32:47,131
Is he just too ambitious?

890
00:32:47,198 --> 00:32:49,067
That's vanilla syrup.

891
00:32:49,133 --> 00:32:51,970
He threw the sweet jelly into milk,
and then some vanilla syrup.

892
00:32:52,036 --> 00:32:54,806
She doesn't have gelatin,
but this comes with agar.

893
00:32:54,872 --> 00:32:56,975
That sweet jelly includes agar,

894
00:32:57,041 --> 00:32:58,943
so it can harden.

895
00:32:59,010 --> 00:33:00,044
That was smart.

896
00:33:00,111 --> 00:33:03,314
However, it does take forever!

897
00:33:03,381 --> 00:33:05,817
It's been a minute already.

898
00:33:05,883 --> 00:33:08,853
-Whoa.
-What's Hyun-suk using? Salmon?

899
00:33:08,920 --> 00:33:10,788
Yes, that's gravlax.

900
00:33:10,855 --> 00:33:13,191
-So it's salmon.
-It's not smoked salmon.

901
00:33:13,257 --> 00:33:14,859
-He's matching the sizes.
-Salmon and cheese?

902
00:33:14,926 --> 00:33:16,260
Yes, it's cheese.

903
00:33:16,327 --> 00:33:19,063
He's stacking layers of salmon and cheese.

904
00:33:19,130 --> 00:33:21,199
He must be trying to make a shape.

905
00:33:21,866 --> 00:33:22,700
D'OH…

906
00:33:22,900 --> 00:33:24,168
NEXT, SALMON!

907
00:33:24,469 --> 00:33:27,138
Your hands have been
trembling a lot more lately.

908
00:33:27,205 --> 00:33:28,639
He can't help it.

909
00:33:28,706 --> 00:33:30,274
His hands have become shakier.

910
00:33:30,341 --> 00:33:33,378
They're shaking more violently.

911
00:33:33,444 --> 00:33:35,146
Put a pain plaster on.

912
00:33:35,213 --> 00:33:38,082
-He's putting burrata in the middle.
-That's burrata?

913
00:33:38,783 --> 00:33:40,518
I guess he'll use lots of that.

914
00:33:40,585 --> 00:33:42,286
What's that?

915
00:33:42,353 --> 00:33:46,090
It's called <i>yuzu kosho,</i>
a sauce made with <i>yuja</i> and pepper.

916
00:33:46,157 --> 00:33:50,094
-I really like that paste.
-It's made with everything you like.

917
00:33:50,161 --> 00:33:52,563
I can't wait to find out what it's like.

918
00:33:53,297 --> 00:33:55,099
Sung-jun is also using salmon.

919
00:33:55,166 --> 00:33:56,868
Sung-jun's using salmon.

920
00:33:56,934 --> 00:33:58,036
I am.

921
00:33:58,102 --> 00:33:59,203
But he's…

922
00:33:59,270 --> 00:34:01,105
CHOPPING!

923
00:34:01,172 --> 00:34:03,074
It's like <i>makhoe</i>, sliced raw fish.

924
00:34:03,141 --> 00:34:04,742
-It's tartar.
-Tartar.

925
00:34:04,809 --> 00:34:06,878
-Tartar.
-Salmon tartar.

926
00:34:07,645 --> 00:34:09,547
Lemon zest.

927
00:34:09,614 --> 00:34:10,548
LEMON JUICE

928
00:34:10,615 --> 00:34:11,516
OLIVE OIL

929
00:34:11,582 --> 00:34:13,151
Is that for the anchovy pasta?

930
00:34:13,217 --> 00:34:14,519
It's the topping.

931
00:34:14,585 --> 00:34:16,254
I see.

932
00:34:16,320 --> 00:34:18,022
It's hard to imagine what it's like.

933
00:34:18,089 --> 00:34:21,726
She really loves salmon.

934
00:34:21,793 --> 00:34:23,061
It's been two minutes,

935
00:34:23,127 --> 00:34:24,896
and apparently Sooyoung loves salmon.

936
00:34:25,530 --> 00:34:26,597
RED PEPPER

937
00:34:26,664 --> 00:34:28,733
Yes, she likes anchovies and salmon.

938
00:34:28,800 --> 00:34:31,102
3. COOK ANCHOVIES, GARLIC,
RED PEPPER, AND CAPERS IN OLIVE OIL

939
00:34:32,370 --> 00:34:34,672
CUT THE SLAB BREAD INTO A ROUND SHAPE

940
00:34:35,506 --> 00:34:37,708
4. COAT THE CIRCULAR BREAD
WITH ANCHOVY OIL AND TOAST

941
00:34:37,775 --> 00:34:39,243
TOASTING IN THE OVEN

942
00:34:40,044 --> 00:34:41,446
SALMON CHEESE ROLL

943
00:34:44,215 --> 00:34:45,950
TURNING 90 DEGREES

944
00:34:46,017 --> 00:34:49,687
I think Hyun-suk wants to roll that,
but it doesn't seem to work.

945
00:34:49,754 --> 00:34:51,889
It is working.

946
00:34:51,956 --> 00:34:54,425
I just got the direction confused.

947
00:34:54,492 --> 00:34:55,493
You're at that age.

948
00:34:56,594 --> 00:34:57,495
FUMING

949
00:34:58,729 --> 00:34:59,697
PLEASE STAY HEALTHY…

950
00:34:59,764 --> 00:35:01,199
How pretty.

951
00:35:01,265 --> 00:35:02,400
It looks like a lobster.

952
00:35:02,767 --> 00:35:04,001
COOKING FOIL

953
00:35:04,068 --> 00:35:06,404
-Huh?
-If he's covering it in foil,

954
00:35:06,471 --> 00:35:07,738
it means he'll cook it somehow.

955
00:35:07,805 --> 00:35:10,141
-In the oven?
-Will you grill it?

956
00:35:10,208 --> 00:35:12,143
-But the cheese will melt.
-He'll cool it down.

957
00:35:13,211 --> 00:35:14,312
It's just for the shape.

958
00:35:14,378 --> 00:35:16,114
-Just the shape?
-Just the shape?

959
00:35:16,180 --> 00:35:19,016
He's just keeping it in shape
and letting it sit.

960
00:35:19,083 --> 00:35:21,052
Sung-jun makes panna cotta.

961
00:35:21,119 --> 00:35:23,688
What's important for panna cotta…

962
00:35:25,523 --> 00:35:27,558
-…is for it to solidify.
-Right.

963
00:35:27,625 --> 00:35:29,727
Because agar doesn't turn solid quickly.

964
00:35:29,794 --> 00:35:32,396
-It takes time.
-It takes a while.

965
00:35:32,463 --> 00:35:34,832
It has to be at a certain temperature.

966
00:35:35,566 --> 00:35:37,101
POURING INTO GLASSES

967
00:35:37,168 --> 00:35:39,637
-So he'll harden them like that?
-But will they?

968
00:35:39,704 --> 00:35:41,839
People are worried over here.

969
00:35:41,906 --> 00:35:43,875
MR. CHESTNUT TIRAMISU'S
CHESTNUT YANGGAENG PANNA COTTA!

970
00:35:44,442 --> 00:35:46,244
HYUN-SUK BEGINS MAKING PASTA DOUGH

971
00:35:46,310 --> 00:35:47,578
I need some salt.

972
00:35:49,514 --> 00:35:50,348
SALT

973
00:35:50,414 --> 00:35:51,349
THIS ISN'T IT!

974
00:35:52,783 --> 00:35:54,018
LET'S ADD THE FLAIR!

975
00:35:54,252 --> 00:35:56,020
I know. That's the flair.

976
00:35:56,087 --> 00:35:58,322
-The hair flip.
-The hair?

977
00:35:58,823 --> 00:36:00,992
SOOYOUNG IS HER GROUP'S CENTER!
I'M THE SHOW'S CENTER!

978
00:36:01,058 --> 00:36:02,693
He'll complain about neck pain next week.

979
00:36:03,661 --> 00:36:06,197
-He's making the pasta dough.
-The pasta dough.

980
00:36:06,264 --> 00:36:07,331
That looks great.

981
00:36:07,398 --> 00:36:09,333
-I hope it turns out nicely.
-It seems so.

982
00:36:09,400 --> 00:36:12,870
-Princess hair. It has to be thin.
-It looks great.

983
00:36:12,937 --> 00:36:15,473
HOW DO YOU POWDER THE DOUGH?

984
00:36:15,973 --> 00:36:17,175
LIKE THIS!

985
00:36:17,542 --> 00:36:18,776
HEARTTHROB

986
00:36:18,843 --> 00:36:21,078
That's the princess's hair flip.

987
00:36:21,646 --> 00:36:22,980
It's his flair show.

988
00:36:23,247 --> 00:36:24,182
WATCH ME!

989
00:36:24,248 --> 00:36:25,116
STAYING TRUE TO THE CONCEPT

