1238
00:45:19,283 --> 00:45:22,352
Both meals are ready for Sooyoung.

1239
00:45:22,419 --> 00:45:25,789
She wanted something really fancy
suitable for a princess.

1240
00:45:25,856 --> 00:45:26,990
Do you like it?

1241
00:45:27,057 --> 00:45:29,526
Just looking at these
already makes me so happy.

1242
00:45:30,160 --> 00:45:31,028
All right.

1243
00:45:31,095 --> 00:45:34,965
First, please try
Chef Hyun-suk's dish first, Choipunzel.

1244
00:45:35,032 --> 00:45:39,303
A SALMON CHEESE ROLL FOR THE PRINCESS

1245
00:45:41,038 --> 00:45:43,807
FRESH SHRIMP CURRY PASTA
REPRESENTING RAPUNZEL'S HAIR

1246
00:45:44,708 --> 00:45:48,612
CHEF CHOI HYUN-SUK'S CHOIPUNZEL

1247
00:45:49,179 --> 00:45:53,283
-It's a salmon and cheese roll.
-It is.

1248
00:45:53,350 --> 00:45:56,320
-And a piece of bread.
-Gosh. I'm so excited.

1249
00:45:56,386 --> 00:45:58,589
Sooyoung looks really excited.

1250
00:45:58,655 --> 00:45:59,990
It's easy to cut.

1251
00:46:00,057 --> 00:46:02,092
-You look like a princess right now.
-Right?

1252
00:46:02,159 --> 00:46:04,528
Yes, even the dish
is something a princess would use.

1253
00:46:05,195 --> 00:46:06,463
ASTONISHED

1254
00:46:06,530 --> 00:46:08,465
-Like the royalty.
-The royalty.

1255
00:46:08,532 --> 00:46:10,267
-What does it smell like?
-Yum.

1256
00:46:10,334 --> 00:46:11,869
THE PRINCESS TAKES HER FIRST BITE

1257
00:46:11,935 --> 00:46:13,303
"Yum"?

1258
00:46:13,370 --> 00:46:15,339
That looks so good.

1259
00:46:16,073 --> 00:46:18,976
-Cheese, salmon, and bread.
-It might be too salty.

1260
00:46:19,042 --> 00:46:19,877
LAUGHING

1261
00:46:19,943 --> 00:46:22,946
It must be good.
She suddenly burst out laughing.

1262
00:46:23,013 --> 00:46:25,349
The princess looks pleased.

1263
00:46:25,415 --> 00:46:26,850
How did he make this?

1264
00:46:27,050 --> 00:46:28,318
COMPLETELY AMAZED

1265
00:46:28,385 --> 00:46:29,987
It's an emergency.

1266
00:46:30,053 --> 00:46:31,922
What's in the roll?

1267
00:46:31,989 --> 00:46:33,657
<i>-Burrata.</i>
<i>-Burrata.</i>

1268
00:46:33,724 --> 00:46:35,893
<i>As well as the </i>yuja<i> pepper paste she had</i>

1269
00:46:35,959 --> 00:46:38,662
<i>to balance out</i>
<i>the saltiness and the richness.</i>

1270
00:46:38,729 --> 00:46:40,597
I became a bit suspicious

1271
00:46:41,098 --> 00:46:42,566
when he added the <i>yuja</i> pepper paste.

1272
00:46:42,633 --> 00:46:44,668
-She said it could be too salty.
-Right.

1273
00:46:44,735 --> 00:46:48,405
It does taste salty,
but this sweetness balances it out.

1274
00:46:48,472 --> 00:46:50,774
She had white balsamic vinegar,

1275
00:46:50,841 --> 00:46:52,075
<i>which can be too sweet.</i>

1276
00:46:52,142 --> 00:46:56,814
<i>So I added some lemon juice</i>
<i>for sourness to make it more appetizing.</i>

1277
00:46:56,880 --> 00:46:57,915
I want another bite.

1278
00:46:57,981 --> 00:46:59,383
-Have more.
-Go ahead.

1279
00:46:59,449 --> 00:47:02,553
These are all your ingredients.

1280
00:47:02,619 --> 00:47:04,321
-I'm so happy.
-You can have it all.

1281
00:47:05,055 --> 00:47:07,157
How did he make this with my ingredients?

1282
00:47:07,958 --> 00:47:10,661
So this is the fun of <i>Chef & My Fridge.</i>

1283
00:47:10,727 --> 00:47:12,629
If you can be bothered a little,

1284
00:47:12,696 --> 00:47:14,565
-you can make that yourself.
-Of course.

1285
00:47:14,631 --> 00:47:17,234
He made that
with everything you had in your fridge.

1286
00:47:17,301 --> 00:47:20,404
-He's turning her into a princess.
-Gosh, it's so good.

1287
00:47:20,470 --> 00:47:23,574
-Next, the pasta.
-It looks good.

1288
00:47:23,640 --> 00:47:27,444
It already tasted perfect
when he had three minutes left.

1289
00:47:27,511 --> 00:47:31,815
He had to flip his hair and everything
to make that pasta.

1290
00:47:32,382 --> 00:47:34,218
Will it please her appetite?

1291
00:47:34,785 --> 00:47:35,619
The princess's…

1292
00:47:35,686 --> 00:47:36,687
-Huh?
-Oh, no.

1293
00:47:37,254 --> 00:47:38,322
ROLLING OFF

1294
00:47:38,388 --> 00:47:39,356
That's mine.

1295
00:47:39,423 --> 00:47:41,291
-This?
-Yours?

1296
00:47:41,358 --> 00:47:42,359
It's hers.

1297
00:47:42,426 --> 00:47:43,560
-That's yours?
-I'll taste it.

1298
00:47:43,627 --> 00:47:46,330
-I picked it up for you.
-Has it been three seconds?

1299
00:47:46,396 --> 00:47:47,464
SLURP

1300
00:47:47,531 --> 00:47:48,866
I wonder what the pasta is like.

1301
00:47:49,800 --> 00:47:51,068
MMM

1302
00:47:52,769 --> 00:47:54,104
It looks good.

1303
00:47:54,171 --> 00:47:57,474
Chef Hyun-suk cranes his neck,
waiting for your response.

1304
00:47:58,041 --> 00:48:00,444
It has a Japanese twist to it.

1305
00:48:00,677 --> 00:48:02,679
A JAPANESE TWIST?

1306
00:48:02,746 --> 00:48:04,848
It's like
a really old restaurant you run into

1307
00:48:04,915 --> 00:48:07,684
in rural Japan,
a place that's really good.

1308
00:48:07,751 --> 00:48:09,086
-Made by a country grandpa.
-Yes.

1309
00:48:09,152 --> 00:48:10,921
So I found this place,

1310
00:48:10,988 --> 00:48:13,724
creaked open the old door,

1311
00:48:13,790 --> 00:48:16,159
and the place only has
one thing on the menu.

1312
00:48:16,226 --> 00:48:17,461
An old country man?

1313
00:48:17,527 --> 00:48:19,263
An old expert.

1314
00:48:19,329 --> 00:48:21,865
So I ordered curry pasta, and…

1315
00:48:22,432 --> 00:48:24,868
<i>Delicious.</i>

1316
00:48:24,935 --> 00:48:26,236
<i>Delish-love you.</i>

1317
00:48:26,303 --> 00:48:27,971
Did you mean to add the Japanese twist?

1318
00:48:28,038 --> 00:48:31,108
The princess is traveling
with her private chef

1319
00:48:31,174 --> 00:48:32,376
to Japan.

1320
00:48:34,311 --> 00:48:36,847
-I love the storyline.
-I knew it.

1321
00:48:36,914 --> 00:48:37,981
Does that mean

1322
00:48:38,048 --> 00:48:40,884
I should consider this dish
a trip to Italy?

1323
00:48:40,951 --> 00:48:42,986
-Where's this? Italy.
-Italy.

1324
00:48:43,053 --> 00:48:45,989
It's like I'm on a cruise ship
going between Italy and Japan.

1325
00:48:47,291 --> 00:48:48,759
-You should've said that.
-That's it.

1326
00:48:48,825 --> 00:48:52,396
A cruise ship that set sail in Italy
and will arrive in Japan.

1327
00:48:52,763 --> 00:48:54,298
THAT'S AN INSANE INTERPRETATION

1328
00:48:54,364 --> 00:48:57,167
I think this dish
has been meticulously planned out.

1329
00:48:57,234 --> 00:49:00,103
Topping salmon on top of grain bread

1330
00:49:00,170 --> 00:49:01,171
is done in North Europe,

1331
00:49:01,238 --> 00:49:03,040
in countries like Denmark.

1332
00:49:03,106 --> 00:49:05,575
And as you mentioned,
this one is more Japanese.

1333
00:49:05,642 --> 00:49:08,078
You know, not many countries
have princesses anymore.

1334
00:49:08,145 --> 00:49:10,714
OH! ARE YOU SAYING…

1335
00:49:10,781 --> 00:49:15,352
He thought of princesses and wanted you
to experience Denmark and Japan.

1336
00:49:15,419 --> 00:49:16,620
<i>-Princess!</i>
-Yes.

1337
00:49:16,687 --> 00:49:19,323
-Was it intentional?
<i>-Is that so?</i>

1338
00:49:19,389 --> 00:49:22,459
-Is this correct?
<i>-Amazing!</i>

1339
00:49:22,960 --> 00:49:23,961
SIGH…

1340
00:49:24,027 --> 00:49:25,495
How did he figure out

1341
00:49:25,562 --> 00:49:26,930
something I wasn't going to share?

1342
00:49:28,265 --> 00:49:29,733
How did you point it out?

1343
00:49:29,800 --> 00:49:31,635
It was for the princess experience.

1344
00:49:31,702 --> 00:49:34,905
Both Japan and Denmark are countries
that still have princesses.

1345
00:49:35,305 --> 00:49:37,240
AND KOREA DOES TOO♥

1346
00:49:37,307 --> 00:49:39,042
-That was sharp.
-I got chills.

1347
00:49:39,109 --> 00:49:41,478
<i>Princess Sooyoung, please.</i>

1348
00:49:42,946 --> 00:49:45,248
That was Chef Hyun-suk's Choipunzel.

1349
00:49:45,315 --> 00:49:47,784
Next, Chef Sung-jun's meal,

1350
00:49:47,851 --> 00:49:49,820
<i>Into Three New Worlds.</i>

1351
00:49:49,886 --> 00:49:51,021
JAMÓN BRUSCHETTA

1352
00:49:51,088 --> 00:49:54,358
ANCHOVY OIL PASTA

1353
00:49:55,425 --> 00:49:57,494
GONGJU CHESTNUT PANNA COTTA

1354
00:49:58,362 --> 00:50:02,532
CHEF KWON SUNG-JUN'S INTO THREE NEW WORLDS

1355
00:50:02,599 --> 00:50:04,968
My dishes have a story.

1356
00:50:05,035 --> 00:50:06,737
A love story with her.

1357
00:50:06,803 --> 00:50:08,238
-Is that so?
-Back there…

1358
00:50:08,305 --> 00:50:09,806
-And she has to hear it first?
-Not me.

1359
00:50:09,873 --> 00:50:11,375
Yes, she needs to hear it a bit.

1360
00:50:11,441 --> 00:50:12,776
I think it'll backfire.

1361
00:50:12,843 --> 00:50:15,178
-He'll kill her appetite.
-Exactly.

1362
00:50:15,245 --> 00:50:16,813
I think he wants to lose.

1363
00:50:16,880 --> 00:50:19,449
Is there a story between you and Sooyoung?

1364
00:50:19,516 --> 00:50:20,350
There is.

1365
00:50:20,417 --> 00:50:23,987
I waited in front of the fridge
while checking the time

1366
00:50:24,054 --> 00:50:27,491
<i>because I was waiting for her</i>
<i>at Yongsan Station, exit three.</i>

1367
00:50:27,557 --> 00:50:29,359
First, I give her a flower.

1368
00:50:30,594 --> 00:50:32,162
In front of Yongsan Station?

1369
00:50:32,229 --> 00:50:34,031
What's he saying?

1370
00:50:34,097 --> 00:50:35,799
Can she eat it now?

1371
00:50:35,866 --> 00:50:37,167
-That flower.
-Yongsan Station?

1372
00:50:37,234 --> 00:50:38,535
So try the appetizer first.

1373
00:50:38,602 --> 00:50:40,737
-The appetizer.
-So I got the flower now?

1374
00:50:40,804 --> 00:50:42,072
-Yes.
-She got it.

1375
00:50:42,139 --> 00:50:42,973
At Yongsan Station.

1376
00:50:43,040 --> 00:50:45,442
Why did it have to be Yongsan Station?

1377
00:50:45,509 --> 00:50:47,277
Because I live in Yongsan-gu.

1378
00:50:48,045 --> 00:50:49,279
He's selfish.

1379
00:50:49,346 --> 00:50:51,615
She must've come to Yongsan.

1380
00:50:51,681 --> 00:50:52,582
He called her over.

1381
00:50:53,150 --> 00:50:55,118
-Is there a ring?
-Is there?

1382
00:50:55,185 --> 00:50:57,521
Try the bread, <i>jamón</i>, and the cheese.

1383
00:50:57,587 --> 00:50:59,856
That flower looks tough.

1384
00:50:59,923 --> 00:51:02,592
-I hope it's not tough.
-Did you want it to be tough?

1385
00:51:02,659 --> 00:51:04,528
-Is that like you?
-It's my tenacious love.

1386
00:51:04,795 --> 00:51:06,063
LOL

1387
00:51:06,129 --> 00:51:08,165
How he loved her through the years.

1388
00:51:08,231 --> 00:51:11,535
But food should never be too tough.

1389
00:51:11,601 --> 00:51:15,105
-But <i>jamón</i> is always a little tough.
-That's how <i>jamón </i>is.

1390
00:51:15,172 --> 00:51:17,007
-What is it?
-Yes?

1391
00:51:17,074 --> 00:51:19,209
-What is it?
-Did you find a ring?

1392
00:51:21,812 --> 00:51:22,813
What's wrong?

1393
00:51:23,146 --> 00:51:24,748
IS THERE A PROBLEM?

1394
00:51:24,815 --> 00:51:25,882
What's wrong?

1395
00:51:27,818 --> 00:51:28,919
HEY

1396
00:51:30,687 --> 00:51:32,856
-You had us scared there.
-Really.

1397
00:51:32,923 --> 00:51:35,392
There was a heart in the dish.

1398
00:51:35,459 --> 00:51:36,860
This is so good.

1399
00:51:37,360 --> 00:51:38,762
FEELING PROUD

1400
00:51:38,829 --> 00:51:41,832
I really love this pistachio spread.

1401
00:51:43,500 --> 00:51:46,503
<i>It's bread, pistachio spread, and </i>jamón.

1402
00:51:46,570 --> 00:51:47,804
<i>A mix of three ingredients.</i>

1403
00:51:47,871 --> 00:51:49,372
It's the kind of flavor I love.

1404
00:51:50,006 --> 00:51:51,741
-He captured her taste.
-All right.

1405
00:51:51,808 --> 00:51:54,311
-Is that olive oil on top?
-Just a drizzle.

1406
00:51:54,377 --> 00:51:56,680
-Bread, <i>jamón</i>, and pistachio.
-Pistachio.

1407
00:51:56,746 --> 00:51:58,648
And a bit of olive oil.

1408
00:51:58,715 --> 00:52:01,318
She's frowning a little.

1409
00:52:01,384 --> 00:52:03,286
That's the frown you show
when you're moved.

1410
00:52:03,353 --> 00:52:05,188
She's starting to clap.

1411
00:52:05,255 --> 00:52:07,290
That was the first dish.

1412
00:52:07,357 --> 00:52:09,326
The second world among the three worlds.

1413
00:52:09,392 --> 00:52:11,161
-It's a date, so we must eat.
-The second.

1414
00:52:11,228 --> 00:52:12,496
-You're eating?
-At a pasta place.

1415
00:52:12,562 --> 00:52:14,564
It's an anchovy pasta.

1416
00:52:14,631 --> 00:52:15,699
Is this seaweed <i>bugak?</i>

1417
00:52:15,765 --> 00:52:18,969
<i>I smashed a few</i>
<i>to add the crunchy texture.</i>

1418
00:52:19,035 --> 00:52:22,973
-It was intentional.
-I think this was Chef Jong-won's <i>bugak.</i>

1419
00:52:23,039 --> 00:52:25,175
-Is that so?
-It is.

1420
00:52:25,242 --> 00:52:26,276
I'm curious.

1421
00:52:26,343 --> 00:52:27,244
I'm so curious.

1422
00:52:27,310 --> 00:52:28,845
-She's curious.
-It should be salty.

1423
00:52:28,912 --> 00:52:31,581
-She loves anchovies.
-She makes pasta at home too.

1424
00:52:33,450 --> 00:52:35,852
She bought the tinned anchovies
because she liked them.

1425
00:52:35,919 --> 00:52:36,987
CHUCKLING

1426
00:52:37,053 --> 00:52:38,088
HEY

1427
00:52:38,155 --> 00:52:39,189
She's starting to giggle.

1428
00:52:39,256 --> 00:52:42,058
-It must be good.
-It must be different from your pasta.

1429
00:52:42,125 --> 00:52:43,293
He's so annoying.

1430
00:52:43,360 --> 00:52:44,728
Look at his face.

1431
00:52:44,794 --> 00:52:45,662
TOTAL ARROGANCE

1432
00:52:45,729 --> 00:52:47,864
This salmon isn't too salty.

1433
00:52:47,931 --> 00:52:50,367
I didn't add lots of salt to the salmon.

1434
00:52:50,433 --> 00:52:53,403
<i>I just added some lemon juice</i>
<i>for some sourness.</i>

1435
00:52:53,470 --> 00:52:57,007
-To boost the umami.
-That was why he added water.

1436
00:52:57,073 --> 00:52:58,475
And some champagne got in there too.

1437
00:52:58,542 --> 00:53:01,511
Yes, it did. There's champagne in there.

1438
00:53:01,578 --> 00:53:03,580
-It worked out.
-He popped the bottle.

1439
00:53:03,647 --> 00:53:07,250
-Unintentionally?
-He unintentionally helped him.

1440
00:53:07,317 --> 00:53:09,452
-I had put some in already.
-You had?

1441
00:53:09,519 --> 00:53:10,787
I think he added more for me.

1442
00:53:10,854 --> 00:53:12,956
Yes, he added more champagne.

1443
00:53:13,023 --> 00:53:14,691
He saw that it could use more sourness,

1444
00:53:14,758 --> 00:53:17,561
so he sacrificed himself
and added more into the dish.

1445
00:53:17,627 --> 00:53:18,461
Isn't that right?

1446
00:53:19,162 --> 00:53:20,063
What?

1447
00:53:20,630 --> 00:53:22,165
Will you listen when I talk?

1448
00:53:22,232 --> 00:53:23,667
Please stop dozing off!

1449
00:53:23,733 --> 00:53:25,035
I was complimenting you.

1450
00:53:25,101 --> 00:53:26,803
-You're right.
-Right?

1451
00:53:26,870 --> 00:53:27,704
-Yes.
-I see.

1452
00:53:27,771 --> 00:53:29,773
He's exhausted.

1453
00:53:29,839 --> 00:53:31,908
-The third dish, panna cotta.
-Panna cotta.

1454
00:53:31,975 --> 00:53:33,643
<i>I mixed chestnut </i>yanggaeng<i> and milk.</i>

1455
00:53:33,710 --> 00:53:36,379
<i>I added oolong tea for aroma</i>
<i>and some vanilla syrup too.</i>

1456
00:53:36,446 --> 00:53:38,515
<i>-Oolong tea.</i>
<i>-And topped it with cream cheese.</i>

1457
00:53:38,582 --> 00:53:41,117
Did you use the tea I had?

1458
00:53:41,184 --> 00:53:42,485
You're right. Oolong tea.

1459
00:53:42,552 --> 00:53:44,521
That is such a wonder.

1460
00:53:45,689 --> 00:53:47,490
He's not allowed to use
any other oolong tea.

1461
00:53:47,557 --> 00:53:49,392
-Yes.
-That's the rule.

1462
00:53:49,459 --> 00:53:51,628
Where are you now?

1463
00:53:51,695 --> 00:53:53,863
-We're at a café now after dinner.
-Going to a café.

1464
00:53:53,930 --> 00:53:55,098
The last stop.

1465
00:53:55,165 --> 00:53:56,566
Yongsan must have great joints.

1466
00:53:56,633 --> 00:53:58,501
It does. That's true.

1467
00:53:59,536 --> 00:54:01,204
PERFECT PUDDING TEXTURE

1468
00:54:01,271 --> 00:54:03,006
He did well until now. The last one.

1469
00:54:03,073 --> 00:54:04,107
YUM

1470
00:54:06,176 --> 00:54:07,644
OH?

1471
00:54:07,911 --> 00:54:09,479
ARROGANCE TAKE 2

1472
00:54:09,546 --> 00:54:10,880
It must be good.

1473
00:54:10,947 --> 00:54:12,782
Why am I drooling so much?

1474
00:54:13,583 --> 00:54:15,051
What's it like?

1475
00:54:15,118 --> 00:54:18,688
It's probably like melted
and re-hardened chestnut <i>yanggaeng</i>.

1476
00:54:18,755 --> 00:54:20,890
But he added oolong tea.

1477
00:54:20,957 --> 00:54:24,160
<i>The harmony between the cheese,</i>
<i>this chestnut flavor,</i>

1478
00:54:24,227 --> 00:54:25,862
<i>and the overall texture</i>

1479
00:54:25,929 --> 00:54:28,098
is nothing but soft and smooth.

1480
00:54:28,164 --> 00:54:31,201
I also don't like it
when something tastes overly sweet,

1481
00:54:31,268 --> 00:54:32,869
but it must be the oolong tea.

1482
00:54:32,936 --> 00:54:34,771
It's so good.

1483
00:54:34,838 --> 00:54:37,440
-Koreans love chestnuts.
-We do.

1484
00:54:37,507 --> 00:54:39,276
She finished everything. All right.

1485
00:54:39,342 --> 00:54:40,777
-Sooyoung.
-Gosh. The Yongsan…

1486
00:54:40,844 --> 00:54:42,779
-The Yongsan date.
-Yongsan date.

1487
00:54:42,846 --> 00:54:44,848
That was a well-thought-out date.

1488
00:54:44,914 --> 00:54:47,684
Now, it's time for you to choose.

1489
00:54:47,751 --> 00:54:49,753
This is hard. It must be.

1490
00:54:49,819 --> 00:54:51,288
<i>Press one for Sung-jun</i>

1491
00:54:51,354 --> 00:54:52,989
<i>and two for Hyun-suk.</i>

1492
00:54:53,056 --> 00:54:54,557
Make your decision

1493
00:54:54,624 --> 00:54:56,426
and please press the button.

1494
00:54:57,494 --> 00:54:58,695
Did you press it?

1495
00:54:58,762 --> 00:55:00,030
Oh, no.

1496
00:55:00,096 --> 00:55:01,898
Oh, no.

1497
00:55:02,832 --> 00:55:03,767
Did you press it?

1498
00:55:03,833 --> 00:55:05,268
She did.

1499
00:55:05,335 --> 00:55:08,305
She came to a decision
and made her choice.

1500
00:55:08,371 --> 00:55:10,974
-It's breaking my heart.
-It's breaking her heart.

1501
00:55:11,041 --> 00:55:13,510
-And because of who?
-Breaking her heart?

1502
00:55:13,576 --> 00:55:17,080
Which meal did she choose?

1503
00:55:17,147 --> 00:55:20,083
Let's find out the result. Show us.

1504
00:55:21,084 --> 00:55:22,585
Rule of the Princess's Dish.

1505
00:55:22,652 --> 00:55:27,190
Is it Sung-jun, who kept Sooyoung
as his bias since the day she debuted?

1506
00:55:27,257 --> 00:55:32,495
Or is it Hyun-suk, who claims
Sooyoung must stand in the middle?

1507
00:55:33,063 --> 00:55:34,864
Who's going to be the winner?

1508
00:55:34,931 --> 00:55:36,933
Can Sung-jun get a second date?

1509
00:55:37,000 --> 00:55:39,402
Who did Sooyoung choose?

1510
00:55:40,370 --> 00:55:43,039
-I'm nervous.
-Who did she choose?

1511
00:55:43,106 --> 00:55:45,442
KWON SUNG-JUN WINS

1512
00:55:45,508 --> 00:55:46,609
INTO THREE NEW WORLDS WINS

1513
00:55:46,676 --> 00:55:47,677
It was Sung-jun.

1514
00:55:48,712 --> 00:55:50,213
Sung-jun wins.

1515
00:55:50,280 --> 00:55:51,781
SOOYOUNG'S HUBBY WINS

1516
00:55:51,848 --> 00:55:53,950
Into Three New Worlds.

1517
00:55:56,019 --> 00:55:57,921
Sung-jun's wish came true.

1518
00:55:57,987 --> 00:56:00,223
And he broke the jinx.

1519
00:56:00,290 --> 00:56:03,026
He had lost all ten cook-offs
involving K-pop stars,

1520
00:56:03,093 --> 00:56:07,764
-It's my first win.
-…but he finally broke his jinx.

1521
00:56:07,831 --> 00:56:10,233
Sooyoung chose you,

1522
00:56:10,300 --> 00:56:13,603
which puts you in a tie
with Hyun-suk at eight stars.

1523
00:56:13,670 --> 00:56:15,538
-Eight stars.
-Eight?

1524
00:56:15,605 --> 00:56:18,241
You have abandoned Chef Hyun-suk

1525
00:56:18,808 --> 00:56:20,977
and chosen Chef Sung-jun, so why?

1526
00:56:21,044 --> 00:56:22,412
"Abandoned"?

1527
00:56:22,479 --> 00:56:26,116
It all came down to this dessert.

1528
00:56:26,182 --> 00:56:28,918
-This was so…
-All dates need a dessert.

1529
00:56:28,985 --> 00:56:31,855
It's so crazy
because I got this chestnut <i>yanggaeng</i>

1530
00:56:31,921 --> 00:56:35,358
a few days ago at a meeting
for a film festival screening.

1531
00:56:35,425 --> 00:56:36,993
There was a whole set.

1532
00:56:37,060 --> 00:56:40,230
Some chose the plain red bean ones
while others took the ones with chestnuts,

1533
00:56:40,296 --> 00:56:42,966
-so I also had taken one of them.
-It was that.

1534
00:56:43,032 --> 00:56:45,502
It's so crazy that he made this with that.

1535
00:56:45,568 --> 00:56:48,171
-That's <i>Chef & My Fridge.</i>
-Exactly.

1536
00:56:48,238 --> 00:56:50,974
This was such a witty dish.

1537
00:56:51,941 --> 00:56:54,077
He definitely has great taste.

1538
00:56:54,811 --> 00:56:55,779
-I do.
-I see.

1539
00:56:56,413 --> 00:56:59,682
But Chef Hyun-suk's pasta
was really delicious too.

1540
00:56:59,749 --> 00:57:02,352
And for that appetizer
with the <i>yuja</i> pepper paste,

1541
00:57:02,419 --> 00:57:05,522
-I'll definitely try to make it myself.
-I see.

1542
00:57:05,588 --> 00:57:08,925
You suffered a loss on your birthday.

1543
00:57:10,126 --> 00:57:10,960
Right, it's his birthday.

1544
00:57:11,027 --> 00:57:13,630
He can't smile
even though it's his birthday.

1545
00:57:14,431 --> 00:57:16,766
The toughest thing for me today

1546
00:57:16,833 --> 00:57:17,867
isn't my loss.

1547
00:57:18,435 --> 00:57:20,403
It's that I must watch him dance again.

1548
00:57:21,404 --> 00:57:22,439
That's true.

1549
00:57:22,505 --> 00:57:25,074
-He'll have to dance.
-He'll get his wish again.

1550
00:57:25,141 --> 00:57:26,843
"Into the New World."

1551
00:57:26,910 --> 00:57:30,346
-Please put a star on him.
-Do I do it? Okay.

1552
00:57:30,413 --> 00:57:32,248
Please give him a star.

1553
00:57:34,451 --> 00:57:36,953
This is Sung-jun's eighth win!

1554
00:57:37,554 --> 00:57:39,289
His wish came true.

1555
00:57:39,355 --> 00:57:42,125
-He gets a star from Sooyoung.
-Thank you.

1556
00:57:42,192 --> 00:57:44,294
-It was so delicious.
-After waiting 20 years.

1557
00:57:44,761 --> 00:57:46,996
HIS WISH CAME TRUE

1558
00:57:48,832 --> 00:57:49,799
Congratulations.

1559
00:57:49,866 --> 00:57:53,803
<i>Now for the second cook-off</i>
<i>played with Sooyoung's ingredients.</i>

1560
00:57:53,870 --> 00:57:57,640
He can't be bothered with anything
except for food, Chef Yoon Nam-no.

1561
00:57:57,707 --> 00:58:02,011
She can't be bothered with anything
except for dancing, Chef Park Eun-yeong.

1562
00:58:02,078 --> 00:58:05,114
I guess Nam-no couldn't be bothered
to win stars this year.

1563
00:58:06,182 --> 00:58:07,717
You have two now, right?

1564
00:58:07,784 --> 00:58:08,751
It's a secret.

1565
00:58:10,153 --> 00:58:10,987
He has two.

1566
00:58:11,054 --> 00:58:13,189
<i>You won in the last episode,</i>
<i>so you have two.</i>

1567
00:58:13,256 --> 00:58:14,724
<i>-Yes.</i>
<i>-At least you won.</i>

1568
00:58:14,791 --> 00:58:16,025
I heard you were thrilled.

1569
00:58:16,092 --> 00:58:18,862
That day,
I had <i>gopchang-jeongol</i> by myself.

1570
00:58:18,928 --> 00:58:20,864
-Really? Alone?
-How adorable.

1571
00:58:20,930 --> 00:58:22,966
-You can eat it alone.
-He's so adorable.

1572
00:58:23,032 --> 00:58:25,502
-He eats when he loses and when he wins.
-And when he wins.

1573
00:58:25,568 --> 00:58:28,238
He has many reasons to eat.

1574
00:58:28,304 --> 00:58:29,839
Eun-yeong is in a pinch right now.

1575
00:58:29,906 --> 00:58:31,374
-Right?
-She picked the wrong guy.

1576
00:58:31,441 --> 00:58:33,042
-She lost four times in a row.
-Four times.

1577
00:58:33,109 --> 00:58:34,410
-She has been down lately.
-Four?

1578
00:58:34,477 --> 00:58:37,981
But you also said
this was a perfect order for you.

1579
00:58:38,047 --> 00:58:40,517
I can also be very lazy sometimes,

1580
00:58:40,583 --> 00:58:42,785
so we have something in common.

1581
00:58:42,852 --> 00:58:44,654
When I lived alone in Hong Kong,

1582
00:58:44,721 --> 00:58:46,523
no one was there to do my laundry.

1583
00:58:46,589 --> 00:58:49,359
So it had been piling up and up,
and in the end,

1584
00:58:49,425 --> 00:58:50,660
I had nothing to wear.

1585
00:58:50,727 --> 00:58:54,397
So I finally decided to do the laundry,
lifted the pile of clothes,

1586
00:58:54,464 --> 00:58:55,732
and they had gone moldy.

1587
00:58:56,466 --> 00:58:57,767
It was that bad?

1588
00:58:57,834 --> 00:58:59,269
That's how far I'll go.

1589
00:58:59,335 --> 00:59:01,104
Excuse me.
That's not laziness. It's gross.

1590
00:59:01,170 --> 00:59:02,505
Why share such a story?

1591
00:59:02,572 --> 00:59:04,440
When I lived in Hong Kong,

1592
00:59:04,507 --> 00:59:06,709
I literally had
mushrooms growing in my bathroom.

1593
00:59:06,776 --> 00:59:08,711
-Wait.
-Eun-yeong.

1594
00:59:08,778 --> 00:59:10,413
Pull yourself together, Eun-yeong.

1595
00:59:10,780 --> 00:59:12,715
SUSPICIONS OF ADDING MSG TO THE STORY

1596
00:59:12,782 --> 00:59:14,817
Mushrooms grew there?

1597
00:59:14,884 --> 00:59:16,719
-I'm not that bad.
-You aren't, right?

1598
00:59:16,786 --> 00:59:18,755
I'm not that bad.

1599
00:59:18,821 --> 00:59:20,924
The fridge owner feels uncomfortable.

1600
00:59:20,990 --> 00:59:23,293
I'm saying that
my laziness is that extreme.

1601
00:59:23,560 --> 00:59:25,628
APPROVED

1602
00:59:25,695 --> 00:59:28,064
-It's your laziness.
-That's true.

1603
00:59:28,131 --> 00:59:30,833
Nam-no, you ended up at a hospital once
because you couldn't be bothered?

1604
00:59:30,900 --> 00:59:32,268
-What?
-What is it?

1605
00:59:32,335 --> 00:59:34,304
One day, I was craving <i>ramyeon.</i>

1606
00:59:34,370 --> 00:59:36,339
So I microwaved it.

1607
00:59:36,406 --> 00:59:38,308
I had thrown in two eggs inside too.

1608
00:59:38,374 --> 00:59:40,143
NO, WAIT…

1609
00:59:40,209 --> 00:59:43,112
-And that egg blew up in my mouth.
-It would.

1610
00:59:43,179 --> 00:59:46,249
So I had to pay 100,000 won
because my mouth got skinned.

1611
00:59:46,916 --> 00:59:49,352
-From a burn?
-I got burnt.

1612
00:59:49,419 --> 00:59:52,722
The egg stayed swollen
when it came out of the microwave.

1613
00:59:52,789 --> 00:59:54,157
It hadn't blown up yet,

1614
00:59:54,223 --> 00:59:56,693
but it must've blown up
the moment he bit into it.

1615
00:59:56,759 --> 00:59:59,896
If he spent time after pulling it out,
getting kimchi, and sitting down,

1616
00:59:59,963 --> 01:00:00,863
it would've been fine.

1617
01:00:00,930 --> 01:00:03,132
This means he ate it
as soon as he took it out.

1618
01:00:03,199 --> 01:00:04,767
He put it in his mouth right away.

1619
01:00:04,834 --> 01:00:08,237
Yes, I ate it right away,
and it blew up with a bang.

1620
01:00:08,304 --> 01:00:10,506
The bowl was still in the microwave.

1621
01:00:10,573 --> 01:00:14,010
-He put his head inside it.
-He ate it right away.

1622
01:00:14,410 --> 01:00:16,079
SUCH A FRIGHTENING STORY

1623
01:00:16,145 --> 01:00:18,114
These stories aren't helping them.

1624
01:00:18,181 --> 01:00:21,017
BUT CAN THEIR DISHES HELP THEM?

1625
01:00:21,851 --> 01:00:23,920
CHEF NAM-NO'S INGREDIENTS:
AVOCADO, MINI CUCUMBER, CHERRY TOMATO

1626
01:00:23,987 --> 01:00:26,022
LEMON, ARUGULA, BURRATA, SEAWEED BUGAK,
CHILI OIL, OYSTER SAUCE, AND MORE

1627
01:00:26,089 --> 01:00:28,124
What are you making, Chef Nam-no?

1628
01:00:28,191 --> 01:00:29,859
I prepared a dish called

1629
01:00:29,926 --> 01:00:32,295
Right Now, It's Nam-no's Generation!

1630
01:00:32,362 --> 01:00:34,097
From now on, it's Nam-no's Generation.

1631
01:00:34,163 --> 01:00:35,498
Forever Nam-no's Generation!

1632
01:00:35,565 --> 01:00:37,066
All right.

1633
01:00:37,266 --> 01:00:38,735
GIRLS' GENERATION IS PLEASED

1634
01:00:38,801 --> 01:00:40,870
-Right Now, It's Nam-no's Generation!
-That was great.

1635
01:00:40,937 --> 01:00:42,805
-So your time is here?
-It is.

1636
01:00:42,872 --> 01:00:45,308
I will not use a knife today.

1637
01:00:45,541 --> 01:00:46,576
SURPRISED

1638
01:00:46,643 --> 01:00:48,378
I will not use a cutting board,

1639
01:00:48,444 --> 01:00:50,213
and I will not use scissors either.

1640
01:00:50,279 --> 01:00:52,382
-That's awesome.
-How will you cut things?

1641
01:00:52,448 --> 01:00:54,217
With your teeth? Is that it?

1642
01:00:54,283 --> 01:00:55,618
-No knives, and no scissors?
-No.

1643
01:00:55,685 --> 01:00:57,053
I prepared two dishes.

1644
01:00:57,120 --> 01:00:58,688
-Two?
-Two?

1645
01:00:58,755 --> 01:01:01,791
First, canapes made with an avocado.

1646
01:01:01,858 --> 01:01:03,426
Canape. He'll mash it.

1647
01:01:03,493 --> 01:01:05,928
Next, I'll make
an easy version of dandan noodles.

1648
01:01:05,995 --> 01:01:08,598
-Dandan noodles?
-That sounds so good.

1649
01:01:08,665 --> 01:01:11,300
Then you'll have to chop the ingredients.

1650
01:01:11,367 --> 01:01:13,770
-Will he chop them?
-Are you using a blender?

1651
01:01:13,836 --> 01:01:16,172
-I will not use a blender.
-What?

1652
01:01:16,239 --> 01:01:17,373
Wait.

1653
01:01:17,440 --> 01:01:18,741
Wait a second.

1654
01:01:18,808 --> 01:01:20,977
You shouldn't complicate it further
by not using any tools.

1655
01:01:21,044 --> 01:01:23,012
-She has a point.
-Yes.

1656
01:01:23,079 --> 01:01:24,313
He had the wrong idea.

1657
01:01:24,380 --> 01:01:26,516
I haven't thought of that.

1658
01:01:27,617 --> 01:01:29,519
Then you won't have too many dirty dishes.

1659
01:01:29,585 --> 01:01:32,188
No, not too many dirty dishes.

1660
01:01:32,255 --> 01:01:33,456
And less labor.

1661
01:01:33,523 --> 01:01:34,857
And less labor.

1662
01:01:34,924 --> 01:01:36,492
It'd be great
if he can make something delicious

1663
01:01:36,559 --> 01:01:39,462
with minimum effort,
and while using fewer dishes.

1664
01:01:39,529 --> 01:01:42,131
The one thing he's using the least now

1665
01:01:42,198 --> 01:01:43,099
is his brain.

1666
01:01:44,467 --> 01:01:45,301
Come on.

1667
01:01:45,368 --> 01:01:48,004
-I will not use my brain.
-You're too harsh.

1668
01:01:48,838 --> 01:01:50,873
CHEF EUN-YEONG'S INGREDIENTS:
BRISKET, SOFT TOFU, TTEOKGUK RICE CAKE

1669
01:01:50,940 --> 01:01:53,009
CHILI OIL, OYSTER SAUCE, CHICKEN STOCK,
BLUEBERRY, PEACH, HONEY, AND MORE

1670
01:01:53,076 --> 01:01:56,079
Up against him is Chef Eun-yeong.
What's your dish?

1671
01:01:56,145 --> 01:01:57,914
My dish is called…

1672
01:01:57,980 --> 01:02:00,950
<i>MicrowaGee, Gee, Gee, Gee, Gee</i>

1673
01:02:01,017 --> 01:02:01,984
Microwa…

1674
01:02:02,051 --> 01:02:03,953
WIPING

1675
01:02:04,320 --> 01:02:05,888
CHEF PARK EUN-YEONG'S MICROWAGEE

1676
01:02:05,955 --> 01:02:07,890
That's awesome.

1677
01:02:07,957 --> 01:02:10,259
Her eyes were normal
while dancing for the first time.

1678
01:02:10,326 --> 01:02:11,794
EYES ARE STILL ALIVE

1679
01:02:11,861 --> 01:02:14,063
I've been enjoying dancing,
so I fixed my eyes.

1680
01:02:14,130 --> 01:02:16,766
But that makes you lose your charm.

1681
01:02:16,833 --> 01:02:20,236
<i>-MicrowaGee, gee, gee, gee</i>
<i>-Baby, baby</i>

1682
01:02:20,303 --> 01:02:23,673
I'm using only the microwave to cook.

1683
01:02:23,740 --> 01:02:24,941
Nothing on the stove.

1684
01:02:25,007 --> 01:02:26,375
That's awesome.

1685
01:02:26,442 --> 01:02:29,512
I also won't use
a knife or a cutting board.

1686
01:02:29,579 --> 01:02:31,280
I'm going to make mapo tofu.

1687
01:02:31,347 --> 01:02:32,515
Mapo tofu?

1688
01:02:32,582 --> 01:02:36,486
It has to boil hard over heat
to be the most delicious,

1689
01:02:36,552 --> 01:02:40,523
but I'll use the microwave
and even add a smoky flavor.

1690
01:02:40,590 --> 01:02:42,125
You can do that with a microwave?

1691
01:02:42,191 --> 01:02:44,460
-I should learn from her.
-So first, mapo tofu.

1692
01:02:44,527 --> 01:02:46,629
And since it's summer,
I'll make blueberry <i>bingsu.</i>

1693
01:02:46,696 --> 01:02:48,931
-I'll throw that in too.
<i>-Bingsu?</i>

1694
01:02:48,998 --> 01:02:50,500
So Nam-no,

1695
01:02:50,566 --> 01:02:51,968
even today, you won't win a star.

1696
01:02:52,034 --> 01:02:54,237
<i>Gee, gee, gee, gee</i>

1697
01:02:54,303 --> 01:02:56,873
Nam-no, even today, you won't win a star.

1698
01:02:56,939 --> 01:02:58,775
Let us begin this cook-off for Sooyoung,

1699
01:02:58,841 --> 01:03:00,109
Don't Skip Meals Because

1700
01:03:00,176 --> 01:03:01,677
-You Can't Be Bothered.
-This is crazy.

1701
01:03:01,744 --> 01:03:02,845
You can do this!

1702
01:03:02,912 --> 01:03:04,747
I'm excited to see
this new genre of dishes.

1703
01:03:04,814 --> 01:03:08,117
This woman can take Nam-no down easily,
without even using the stove,

1704
01:03:08,184 --> 01:03:09,285
Chef Park Eun-yeong.

1705
01:03:09,352 --> 01:03:10,987
This guy will chop Eun-yeong into pieces

1706
01:03:11,053 --> 01:03:13,289
without any knives or scissors,

1707
01:03:13,356 --> 01:03:15,591
Chef Yoon Nam-no.

1708
01:03:15,658 --> 01:03:19,028
Which chef will the lazy Sooyoung choose?

1709
01:03:19,095 --> 01:03:22,165
Let the 15-minute cook-off begin!

1710
01:03:25,134 --> 01:03:26,068
Begin!

1711
01:03:26,135 --> 01:03:27,970
A DISH FOR THE LAZY PERSON

1712
01:03:28,971 --> 01:03:30,306
NAM-NO CUTS AN AVOCADO

1713
01:03:30,373 --> 01:03:32,008
Is that a knife?

1714
01:03:32,074 --> 01:03:32,975
It's a spatula.

1715
01:03:33,543 --> 01:03:34,844
Wait.

1716
01:03:34,911 --> 01:03:36,512
-Come on.
-Come on.

1717
01:03:36,579 --> 01:03:38,381
Just use scissors instead.

1718
01:03:38,447 --> 01:03:39,849
-Boo.
-Why?

1719
01:03:39,916 --> 01:03:42,318
She's really using scissors.

1720
01:03:42,385 --> 01:03:44,554
She's not using a knife. Only scissors.

1721
01:03:44,620 --> 01:03:46,989
That's literally how I cut green onions.

1722
01:03:47,990 --> 01:03:49,058
-She's doing that.
-Yes.

1723
01:03:49,292 --> 01:03:50,493
WHAT ABOUT NAM-NO AND THE SPATULA?

1724
01:03:50,960 --> 01:03:52,862
CHOPPING OFF MINI CUCUMBER TIPS

1725
01:03:52,929 --> 01:03:53,763
CHUCKLING IN DISBELIEF

1726
01:03:53,830 --> 01:03:55,031
Look what he's doing.

1727
01:03:55,097 --> 01:03:56,999
It's a strongman's show.

1728
01:03:57,066 --> 01:03:58,935
AVOCADO

1729
01:03:59,001 --> 01:04:01,037
-Huh?
-Huh? It's spoiled.

1730
01:04:01,270 --> 01:04:02,705
THE AVOCADO IS SPOILED

1731
01:04:02,772 --> 01:04:05,007
-The avocado went bad.
-Is it spoiled?

1732
01:04:05,074 --> 01:04:06,943
-Has it gone bad?
-Yes.

1733
01:04:07,009 --> 01:04:09,011
Emergency.

1734
01:04:09,078 --> 01:04:11,080
-That's not good.
-It's one of his key ingredients.

1735
01:04:11,147 --> 01:04:12,949
-What about that one?
-What a relief.

1736
01:04:13,015 --> 01:04:14,016
One of them was fine.

1737
01:04:14,350 --> 01:04:15,852
RELIEVED

1738
01:04:15,918 --> 01:04:17,887
Thank god that one was fine.

1739
01:04:17,954 --> 01:04:19,555
1. PREP AN AVOCADO

1740
01:04:19,622 --> 01:04:21,257
-It would've been all over.
-It would've been bad.

1741
01:04:21,490 --> 01:04:22,325
SNIP

1742
01:04:22,725 --> 01:04:23,559
SNIP

1743
01:04:23,826 --> 01:04:25,127
STILL CUTTING THE GREEN ONION…

1744
01:04:25,194 --> 01:04:27,530
-Wait, Chef Eun-yeong.
-Chef Eun-yeong.

1745
01:04:27,597 --> 01:04:29,298
Just use a knife.

1746
01:04:29,365 --> 01:04:32,268
-Using a knife would've been faster.
-It would've been faster.

1747
01:04:32,335 --> 01:04:33,836
-No.
-She's just…

1748
01:04:33,903 --> 01:04:35,605
You can use a knife.

1749
01:04:35,671 --> 01:04:36,973
She's telling you to use it.

1750
01:04:37,039 --> 01:04:39,942
They'll start to hurt her grip very soon.

1751
01:04:40,443 --> 01:04:41,711
-Using a knife…
-How tough.

1752
01:04:41,777 --> 01:04:44,046
-…also means using a board.
-It's not like Sooyoung said

1753
01:04:44,113 --> 01:04:46,549
you aren't allowed to use a knife.

1754
01:04:46,616 --> 01:04:48,384
-I never said that.
-Exactly.

1755
01:04:48,451 --> 01:04:49,986
BANGING

1756
01:04:51,020 --> 01:04:52,088
He's using a stick.

1757
01:04:52,321 --> 01:04:53,689
CRUSHING MINI CUCUMBERS WITH A STICK

1758
01:04:53,756 --> 01:04:55,191
He's using lots of tools.

1759
01:04:55,258 --> 01:04:57,260
Do you have that stick at home, Sooyoung?

1760
01:04:57,326 --> 01:04:59,428
-No, I don't.
-Jeez.

1761
01:04:59,495 --> 01:05:01,197
-Should've used your fist.
-Use your fist.

1762
01:05:02,365 --> 01:05:03,633
You're using your fist?

1763
01:05:03,699 --> 01:05:05,034
He's smashing them with his fist.

1764
01:05:05,101 --> 01:05:06,102
2. SMASH MINI CUCUMBERS WITH YOUR FIST(?)

1765
01:05:06,168 --> 01:05:08,671
Sooyoung doesn't have that stick at home.

1766
01:05:08,738 --> 01:05:10,406
That'll hurt your hands more!

1767
01:05:10,473 --> 01:05:12,208
Just use the back of a knife.

1768
01:05:12,275 --> 01:05:15,077
What's he doing now?
Giving a Thai massage?

1769
01:05:15,144 --> 01:05:16,078
Guys.

1770
01:05:16,145 --> 01:05:17,580
Just use a board and a knife.

1771
01:05:18,948 --> 01:05:22,385
-To cut down on dirty dishes.
-I feel anxious without a cutting board.

1772
01:05:22,451 --> 01:05:25,788
They're doing it all in a pan.

1773
01:05:25,855 --> 01:05:27,957
Instead of using tools,

1774
01:05:28,024 --> 01:05:31,427
they're trying to get things done
using their own bodies.

1775
01:05:31,494 --> 01:05:33,095
Yes. It's been two minutes.

1776
01:05:33,162 --> 01:05:37,700
It looks like there's more labor involved.

1777
01:05:38,501 --> 01:05:39,869
JIFFY NAM-NO

1778
01:05:39,936 --> 01:05:40,770
What do you want?

1779
01:05:40,836 --> 01:05:43,039
-Chili oil.
-Chili oil?

1780
01:05:43,572 --> 01:05:44,407
Vinegar?

1781
01:05:44,473 --> 01:05:45,441
Vinegar.

1782
01:05:45,508 --> 01:05:46,609
3. MIX CUCUMBER WITH CONDIMENTS

1783
01:05:46,676 --> 01:05:48,077
CUCUMBER SALAD SEASONING, FINISHED

1784
01:05:48,444 --> 01:05:50,012
ALSO DONE WITH MAPO TOFU SEASONING

1785
01:05:51,580 --> 01:05:52,515
INTO THE MICROWAGEE

1786
01:05:52,581 --> 01:05:53,716
It's going in.

1787
01:05:54,216 --> 01:05:55,718
GRABS THE SCISSORS AGAIN

1788
01:05:59,622 --> 01:06:00,957
Eun-yeong, just use a knife.

1789
01:06:01,023 --> 01:06:02,725
-Just use a knife already.
-No.

1790
01:06:02,792 --> 01:06:04,493
-Just use a knife.
-Just use it.

1791
01:06:04,560 --> 01:06:06,462
People who can't be bothered

1792
01:06:06,529 --> 01:06:08,364
-never use a knife.
-It's uncomfortable to watch!

1793
01:06:08,431 --> 01:06:10,633
-It's uncomfortable to watch.
-It is.

1794
01:06:10,700 --> 01:06:12,535
It's making us feel uncomfortable.

1795
01:06:13,536 --> 01:06:14,603
CHERRY TOMATOES IN A BAG

1796
01:06:14,670 --> 01:06:16,238
-Tomatoes?
-Tomatoes.

1797
01:06:16,305 --> 01:06:17,974
Will he beat those too?

1798
01:06:18,040 --> 01:06:20,710
You might pop the bag,
so you'd better be careful.

1799
01:06:20,776 --> 01:06:23,346
He's pressing it down
with his body weight.

1800
01:06:23,412 --> 01:06:26,983
Can Sooyoung also put in that much power?

1801
01:06:27,049 --> 01:06:28,617
To press with that much power,

1802
01:06:28,684 --> 01:06:30,486
she needs to jump off the first floor.

1803
01:06:30,553 --> 01:06:32,021
1ST FLOOR, LIKE JUMPING IN PLACE?

1804
01:06:32,955 --> 01:06:34,857
He added white balsamic vinegar.

1805
01:06:35,992 --> 01:06:37,960
NEXT, BOIL NOODLES!

1806
01:06:38,027 --> 01:06:39,428
-Is he cooking <i>ramyeon?</i>
-He is.

1807
01:06:41,597 --> 01:06:42,598
TWO PORTIONS OF THE NOODLES

1808
01:06:43,065 --> 01:06:44,333
How many are you making?

1809
01:06:44,400 --> 01:06:45,701
Don't cook for yourself again.

1810
01:06:45,768 --> 01:06:48,237
We told you
not to cook for yourself again.

1811
01:06:48,304 --> 01:06:50,439
-Wait, how many? Four?
-Four?

1812
01:06:50,506 --> 01:06:52,208
Think before you act!

1813
01:06:52,908 --> 01:06:54,677
Hey, think before you add those.

1814
01:06:54,744 --> 01:06:56,812
The more noodles, the more delicious.

1815
01:06:56,879 --> 01:06:58,714
Don't make it the way you usually do.

1816
01:06:58,781 --> 01:07:00,282
He can eat four bags of it?

1817
01:07:01,550 --> 01:07:03,519
WHY DOES EUN-YEONG
SEEM SO RELAXED IN COMPARISON?

1818
01:07:03,586 --> 01:07:04,420
She's chill.

1819
01:07:04,487 --> 01:07:06,155
You must need lots of starch.

1820
01:07:06,222 --> 01:07:07,590
Why do you need that?

1821
01:07:07,656 --> 01:07:10,559
I have to add it to mapo tofu
to make it thicker.

1822
01:07:10,626 --> 01:07:13,262
-It's for the thickness.
-The thickness.

1823
01:07:13,329 --> 01:07:16,665
She usually has to throw that in
while the soup boils hard,

1824
01:07:16,732 --> 01:07:21,137
so it'll be difficult for her
to take it out, pour, and put it back in.

1825
01:07:21,637 --> 01:07:23,039
GRANDPA, I'LL SHOW YOU!

1826
01:07:26,175 --> 01:07:29,178
-Is that the mapo tofu sauce?
-Yes, it's the sauce.

1827
01:07:30,679 --> 01:07:32,081
OYSTER SAUCE, CHICKEN STOCK, SOY SAUCE

1828
01:07:32,148 --> 01:07:33,816
That's a nice color.

1829
01:07:33,883 --> 01:07:36,519
Isn't it too thin for a mapo tofu sauce?

1830
01:07:36,585 --> 01:07:38,988
-She'll add starch.
-Oh, she'll use starch?

1831
01:07:39,055 --> 01:07:41,557
Starch will cook right away
when it goes into hot water.

1832
01:07:41,624 --> 01:07:43,592
Just mix it well.

1833
01:07:43,659 --> 01:07:46,028
-It'll gelatinize when it's warm enough.
-Really?

1834
01:07:46,095 --> 01:07:48,264
-About 75°C should be enough.
-Is that okay?

1835
01:07:48,330 --> 01:07:50,232
STARCH GELATINIZATION WORKS WELL AT 75°C

1836
01:07:51,667 --> 01:07:53,002
He's actually making <i>ramyeon.</i>

1837
01:07:53,069 --> 01:07:54,603
He's adding the flakes.

1838
01:07:54,670 --> 01:07:56,038
He's just making <i>ramyeon.</i>

1839
01:07:56,105 --> 01:07:57,306
Are you making <i>ramyeon?</i>

1840
01:07:57,373 --> 01:07:59,341
I am. She has no other noodles.

1841
01:07:59,408 --> 01:08:01,310
SETS THE TIMER FOR THE NOODLES

1842
01:08:01,377 --> 01:08:02,311
Oyster sauce.

1843
01:08:02,378 --> 01:08:03,946
-Dandan noodles?
-Oyster sauce.

1844
01:08:04,013 --> 01:08:04,980
Chicken stock.

1845
01:08:05,281 --> 01:08:06,115
ONE RAMYEON SOUP BASE

1846
01:08:06,715 --> 01:08:08,184
Hey, it's a peanut sauce.

1847
01:08:08,250 --> 01:08:09,585
He added peanut butter.

1848
01:08:09,885 --> 01:08:11,353
SOY SAUCE, SUGAR, SESAME OIL

1849
01:08:12,021 --> 01:08:13,255
DANDAN NOODLE SAUCE IS READY

1850
01:08:13,322 --> 01:08:14,557
Eight minutes.

1851
01:08:14,623 --> 01:08:15,524
Seriously?

1852
01:08:15,591 --> 01:08:17,526
You now have eight minutes.

1853
01:08:18,394 --> 01:08:20,396
STILL WORKING ON THE STARCH GELATINIZATION

1854
01:08:20,796 --> 01:08:22,431
THE SAUCE BECAME THICKER

1855
01:08:22,498 --> 01:08:24,033
That seems like a bigger hassle.

1856
01:08:24,100 --> 01:08:25,234
It's not.

1857
01:08:25,301 --> 01:08:27,002
You would've been done if you used a pan.

1858
01:08:27,069 --> 01:08:29,672
To prevent her from skipping meals
because she can't be bothered,

1859
01:08:29,738 --> 01:08:32,041
-the recipe needs to be simple.
-Right.

1860
01:08:32,108 --> 01:08:33,442
They're just not using tools.

1861
01:08:33,509 --> 01:08:36,612
They're both putting in too much work.

1862
01:08:36,679 --> 01:08:39,048
You won't see
any dirty dishes on this side.

1863
01:08:39,115 --> 01:08:40,716
Right. You have a point.

1864
01:08:40,783 --> 01:08:42,585
She'll just eat it and that'll be it.

1865
01:08:42,651 --> 01:08:45,488
-Also, add some <i>tteok</i>, rice cake.
-Rice cake?

1866
01:08:45,554 --> 01:08:47,490
That'll make the sauce too thick.

1867
01:08:47,556 --> 01:08:48,824
It'll become too thick.

1868
01:08:48,891 --> 01:08:50,025
She'll add tofu.

1869
01:08:50,092 --> 01:08:52,027
-It adds water.
-Just like that.

1870
01:08:52,094 --> 01:08:53,963
It looks like mapo tofu.

1871
01:08:54,029 --> 01:08:56,932
-Are you going to microwave it again?
-I will.

1872
01:08:56,999 --> 01:08:58,467
It'd be better to use a pan.

1873
01:08:58,534 --> 01:08:59,768
Yes, it would've been better.

1874
01:09:01,170 --> 01:09:02,471
BACK INTO THE MICROWAVE

1875
01:09:02,538 --> 01:09:03,439
BEEP

1876
01:09:03,506 --> 01:09:04,340
THE NOODLES ARE DONE

1877
01:09:04,406 --> 01:09:06,408
Four portions of <i>ramyeon</i> noodles
are ready.

1878
01:09:06,475 --> 01:09:08,010
-Four servings.
-Four.

1879
01:09:08,077 --> 01:09:09,378
Why did he make so much?

1880
01:09:09,445 --> 01:09:11,680
He's getting paid right now.

1881
01:09:12,715 --> 01:09:15,551
-Will he just use the noodles?
-He'll mix them with the sauce,

1882
01:09:15,618 --> 01:09:16,685
dandan noodle sauce.

1883
01:09:16,752 --> 01:09:18,154
That's a hefty amount just for tasting.

1884
01:09:18,554 --> 01:09:21,056
5. COOL COOKED RAMYEON IN COLD WATER

1885
01:09:21,123 --> 01:09:23,659
-Just the noodles?
-He'll mix them with the sauce.

1886
01:09:23,726 --> 01:09:24,560
It's hot.

1887
01:09:24,627 --> 01:09:25,995
IMMERSION BLENDER

1888
01:09:26,061 --> 01:09:26,896
Wait a second!

1889
01:09:26,962 --> 01:09:28,330
-Why did she pull that out?
-What?

1890
01:09:28,397 --> 01:09:29,965
She picked up an immersion blender.

1891
01:09:31,100 --> 01:09:32,201
FROZEN BLUEBERRIES

1892
01:09:32,268 --> 01:09:33,869
-For the <i>bingsu.</i>
<i>-Bingsu.</i>

1893
01:09:33,936 --> 01:09:35,004
<i>-Bingsu.</i>
-Listen.

1894
01:09:35,070 --> 01:09:38,741
Either eat this one
or the microwaved dish.

1895
01:09:38,807 --> 01:09:40,476
You'll use only one cooking tool.

1896
01:09:42,111 --> 01:09:43,045
FROZEN BLUEBERRIES

1897
01:09:43,112 --> 01:09:44,180
They're frozen.

1898
01:09:44,246 --> 01:09:45,514
You kept them frozen.

1899
01:09:45,581 --> 01:09:46,615
It's to make <i>bingsu.</i>

1900
01:09:46,682 --> 01:09:49,652
-That freezer works well.
-It does.

1901
01:09:50,319 --> 01:09:51,787
EPISODE 78, THE BINGSU IN THE FREEZER

1902
01:09:51,854 --> 01:09:53,289
It melted more in the freezer.

1903
01:09:53,622 --> 01:09:55,691
IT TURNED INTO BINGO MANGSU…

1904
01:09:55,758 --> 01:09:58,427
-That freezer works well.
-It does.

1905
01:09:58,494 --> 01:10:00,462
Last time, we ended up
with <i>hwachae</i>, fruit punch.

1906
01:10:00,896 --> 01:10:01,830
BEGINS TO MAKE BINGSU

1907
01:10:01,897 --> 01:10:03,065
What did you just add?

1908
01:10:03,132 --> 01:10:04,967
-Cream cheese?
-I added cream cheese.

1909
01:10:05,034 --> 01:10:06,368
This is honey.

1910
01:10:06,435 --> 01:10:08,070
Honey and milk.

1911
01:10:08,137 --> 01:10:09,505
That has to be good.

1912
01:10:09,572 --> 01:10:11,307
It'll turn out like ice cream.

1913
01:10:11,373 --> 01:10:13,075
-Really?
-It's frozen now.

1914
01:10:13,142 --> 01:10:14,710
That looks so good.

1915
01:10:15,110 --> 01:10:19,648
4. BLEND BLUEBERRIES,
CREAM CHEESE, HONEY, AND MILK

1916
01:10:21,784 --> 01:10:23,452
She's adding an egg.

1917
01:10:23,519 --> 01:10:24,353
Will you blow it up?

1918
01:10:24,420 --> 01:10:25,955
-What?
-An egg in mapo tofu?

1919
01:10:26,021 --> 01:10:27,489
Will she blow it up to make it smoky?

1920
01:10:28,057 --> 01:10:29,024
It's going in.

1921
01:10:30,059 --> 01:10:32,528
I have a bad feeling.
I think the egg will blow up.

1922
01:10:32,595 --> 01:10:36,065
I learned today that
microwaving an egg will make it blow up.

1923
01:10:36,131 --> 01:10:38,067
-Really? It blows up.
-It does.

1924
01:10:38,133 --> 01:10:38,968
The yolk blows up.

1925
01:10:39,501 --> 01:10:41,770
NAM-NO IS STILL COOLING THE NOODLES

1926
01:10:41,837 --> 01:10:44,273
It would've cooled down by now
if you made just one serving<i>.</i>

1927
01:10:44,340 --> 01:10:45,975
-But he made four.
-This is crazy.

1928
01:10:46,041 --> 01:10:48,711
Five minutes left.
Please check the dishes, Jung-hwan.

1929
01:10:48,777 --> 01:10:50,346
-You have to hurry.
-Oh, gosh.

1930
01:10:51,213 --> 01:10:52,114
OH, NO…

1931
01:10:52,181 --> 01:10:54,950
It's not so easy to cook
without a knife, a cutting board,

1932
01:10:55,017 --> 01:10:56,685
or even the stove.

1933
01:10:56,752 --> 01:10:58,587
But they're somehow managing.

1934
01:10:58,654 --> 01:10:59,788
Will that turn into <i>bingsu?</i>

1935
01:10:59,855 --> 01:11:01,190
Mmm. It's so good.

1936
01:11:01,257 --> 01:11:03,392
Is it really?
It doesn't look like <i>bingsu</i> to me.

1937
01:11:03,459 --> 01:11:05,628
It'll probably taste like a smoothie.

1938
01:11:05,694 --> 01:11:07,863
-Shouldn't you put it in the freezer?
-It's going in.

1939
01:11:07,930 --> 01:11:09,598
INTO THE FREEZER FOR A MOMENT

1940
01:11:09,665 --> 01:11:11,533
Should I try the blueberry <i>bingsu?</i>

1941
01:11:11,600 --> 01:11:12,668
Yes.

1942
01:11:12,735 --> 01:11:14,169
Blueberry smoothie.

1943
01:11:14,236 --> 01:11:16,905
A cold treat for the summer,
blueberry <i>bingsu.</i>

1944
01:11:16,972 --> 01:11:19,508
Is it good enough
to end her four-loss streak?

1945
01:11:19,808 --> 01:11:22,111
SO?

1946
01:11:22,177 --> 01:11:23,379
…four-loss streak?

1947
01:11:23,445 --> 01:11:24,446
It is.

1948
01:11:27,549 --> 01:11:28,684
Will she finally win?

1949
01:11:28,751 --> 01:11:31,687
-It's perfect for this weather.
-Really?

1950
01:11:31,754 --> 01:11:33,922
-It's amazing.
-Really?

1951
01:11:33,989 --> 01:11:35,190
What's this smell?

1952
01:11:35,257 --> 01:11:37,660
It has more flavor
because I added cream cheese.

1953
01:11:37,726 --> 01:11:41,030
It tastes luxurious,
thanks to the cream cheese.

1954
01:11:41,096 --> 01:11:42,798
That's a great tip.

1955
01:11:43,265 --> 01:11:44,900
LET'S GO, YOON NAM-NO!

1956
01:11:45,100 --> 01:11:49,238
6. MIX AVOCADO, AVOCADO OIL,
OLIVE OIL, SALT, AND WASABI

1957
01:11:49,305 --> 01:11:51,106
TO MAKE AVOCADO MOUSSE

1958
01:11:52,474 --> 01:11:55,177
-Nam-no starts plating his food.
-Yoon Nam-no.

1959
01:11:56,278 --> 01:11:59,114
A FINAL TOUCH WITH LEMON ZEST

1960
01:11:59,181 --> 01:12:00,349
Can you put this out?

1961
01:12:00,416 --> 01:12:02,885
-Nam-no is done with something.
-Canapes.

1962
01:12:02,951 --> 01:12:05,120
All he needs to serve now
are the dandan noodles.

1963
01:12:05,521 --> 01:12:07,256
MEANWHILE, PARK EUN-YEONG…

1964
01:12:07,656 --> 01:12:10,025
SHE'S CUTTING A PEACH WITH SCISSORS…

1965
01:12:10,392 --> 01:12:12,928
-Just use a knife.
-Please.

1966
01:12:12,995 --> 01:12:15,931
People who can't be bothered
don't want to use too many tools.

1967
01:12:15,998 --> 01:12:19,702
Just use a knife! Please!

1968
01:12:19,768 --> 01:12:21,303
You're making us uncomfortable.

1969
01:12:21,370 --> 01:12:24,273
I feel like it's all my fault
for saying I'm lazy.

1970
01:12:24,340 --> 01:12:27,076
I'll have to use a cutting board,
which lazy people don't.

1971
01:12:27,142 --> 01:12:30,446
Watch your hands.
Chefs need to take care of their hands.

1972
01:12:31,447 --> 01:12:33,916
DROPPING THE DANDAN NOODLE SAUCE
INTO THE NOODLES

1973
01:12:34,149 --> 01:12:37,986
Nam-no is working with <i>ramyeon…</i>
What did you add to this?

1974
01:12:38,053 --> 01:12:39,555
I made a peanut butter sauce.

1975
01:12:39,621 --> 01:12:41,023
Peanut butter sauce?

1976
01:12:41,390 --> 01:12:42,458
LOTS OF NOODLES

1977
01:12:42,725 --> 01:12:44,159
7. TOP WITH BURRATA AND ARUGULA

1978
01:12:44,226 --> 01:12:46,528
It almost looks like a pasta.

1979
01:12:46,595 --> 01:12:48,130
Is that arugula?

1980
01:12:48,197 --> 01:12:49,998
Try it and see if it's seasoned well.

1981
01:12:50,065 --> 01:12:51,066
Let me do that.

1982
01:12:51,133 --> 01:12:53,602
Is it seasoned well?
He made a lot of noodles.

1983
01:12:53,669 --> 01:12:55,404
-He's trying the noodles.
-He'll add something.

1984
01:12:55,471 --> 01:12:57,740
-Jung-hwan.
-Yes?

1985
01:12:57,806 --> 01:12:58,774
Here I go.

1986
01:12:59,441 --> 01:13:01,243
Now, so?

1987
01:13:01,310 --> 01:13:03,545
Will Nam-no's generation finally come?

1988
01:13:03,612 --> 01:13:05,681
Will Nam-no's generation finally come?

1989
01:13:06,548 --> 01:13:08,417
It's right now.

1990
01:13:08,484 --> 01:13:09,718
It's right now.

1991
01:13:11,286 --> 01:13:13,255
RIGHT NOW, IT'S NAM-NO'S GENERATION!

1992
01:13:13,322 --> 01:13:15,524
-It's Nam-no's generation.
-It is?

1993
01:13:15,591 --> 01:13:17,292
The peanut taste goes so well with this.

1994
01:13:19,061 --> 01:13:21,196
8. TOP NOODLES WITH CHILI OIL
AND CRUSHED SEAWEED BUGAK

1995
01:13:21,263 --> 01:13:23,298
But it's not spicy.

1996
01:13:23,365 --> 01:13:25,200
-It's mostly sweet and nutty.
-He'll add chili oil.

1997
01:13:25,267 --> 01:13:26,869
He just added chili oil.

1998
01:13:26,935 --> 01:13:29,471
So he just added it.
I tried only the noodles.

1999
01:13:29,538 --> 01:13:31,039
This is amazing.

2000
01:13:31,306 --> 01:13:32,274
DAZED…

2001
01:13:32,341 --> 01:13:34,843
-Why are you standing around, Eun-yeong?
-Right now?

2002
01:13:34,910 --> 01:13:36,145
The microwave should be done.

2003
01:13:36,211 --> 01:13:38,714
People who can't be bothered
don't work tirelessly like him.

2004
01:13:38,781 --> 01:13:40,916
-They dance and take it slow.
-She's dancing.

2005
01:13:40,983 --> 01:13:43,218
She's addicted to dancing.

2006
01:13:43,285 --> 01:13:44,119
-What are you up to?
-Go away.

2007
01:13:44,186 --> 01:13:45,287
-Please!
-Why?

2008
01:13:45,354 --> 01:13:47,790
-What's up?
-Just go away.

2009
01:13:47,856 --> 01:13:49,458
-Go to your spot.
-She's bothering him.

2010
01:13:49,525 --> 01:13:51,260
Only Nam-no's working like crazy.

2011
01:13:51,326 --> 01:13:52,661
Can you take this?

2012
01:13:53,896 --> 01:13:55,964
It's time to wrap up. 50 seconds.

2013
01:13:56,265 --> 01:13:57,666
ONLY CUCUMBER SALAD REMAINS

2014
01:13:58,500 --> 01:13:59,334
SESAME

2015
01:14:00,669 --> 01:14:01,670
BALSAMIC TOMATOES

2016
01:14:01,737 --> 01:14:03,372
Thirty seconds.

2017
01:14:03,439 --> 01:14:04,873
-He's done.
-Nam-no is done.

2018
01:14:04,940 --> 01:14:06,208
RIGHT NOW, IT'S NAM-NO'S GENERATION
IS DONE FIRST

2019
01:14:06,275 --> 01:14:07,543
Nam-no is done.

2020
01:14:07,609 --> 01:14:08,811
-Hurry.
-Twenty seconds.

2021
01:14:08,877 --> 01:14:10,212
Eun-yeong has enough time.

2022
01:14:10,279 --> 01:14:11,747
Hurry up. Time's almost up.

2023
01:14:11,814 --> 01:14:14,516
Hurry up. 20 seconds.

2024
01:14:14,583 --> 01:14:16,919
-Ten seconds.
-It's almost time now. Ten.

2025
01:14:16,985 --> 01:14:18,754
-Nine. Eight.
-Eight.

2026
01:14:18,821 --> 01:14:21,557
-Seven. Six. Five.
-The microwave.

2027
01:14:21,623 --> 01:14:23,292
-Seven. Six. Five.
-Hurry.

2028
01:14:23,358 --> 01:14:24,693
-The microwave.
-The microwave.

2029
01:14:24,760 --> 01:14:26,795
-Four. Three.
-Three.

2030
01:14:26,862 --> 01:14:28,597
-Two. One.
-Two. One.

2031
01:14:28,664 --> 01:14:30,666
-Time's up.
-You have to finish up, Eun-yeong.

2032
01:14:31,233 --> 01:14:32,835
Okay. Chef Eun-yeong is done.

2033
01:14:33,302 --> 01:14:36,071
MICROWAGEE IS FINISHED TOO

2034
01:14:36,138 --> 01:14:37,806
It smells like <i>sundubu-jjigae,</i>
soft tofu stew.

2035
01:14:37,873 --> 01:14:40,976
It's somewhere between
<i>sundubu-jjigae</i> and mapo tofu.

2036
01:14:41,043 --> 01:14:42,811
I love that.

2037
01:14:42,878 --> 01:14:44,913
The egg hasn't been cooked.

2038
01:14:44,980 --> 01:14:46,682
-Did she cover it up with sesame?
-She did.

2039
01:14:46,748 --> 01:14:47,883
She covered it up.

2040
01:14:47,950 --> 01:14:49,585
That's a smart move.

2041
01:14:49,651 --> 01:14:50,486
What did she hide?

2042
01:14:50,552 --> 01:14:52,020
Once you mix it, it'll cook.

2043
01:14:52,087 --> 01:14:53,455
It was intentional.

2044
01:14:53,789 --> 01:14:55,591
NAM-NO EATS THE LEFTOVER NOODLES

2045
01:14:55,824 --> 01:14:57,192
SO GOOD

2046
01:14:57,259 --> 01:15:00,696
And now, both dishes
are ready for Sooyoung.

2047
01:15:00,963 --> 01:15:03,599
AMAZED

2048
01:15:03,665 --> 01:15:06,468
It's amazing that they did this
without using too many tools.

2049
01:15:07,803 --> 01:15:09,238
I'm so excited right now.

2050
01:15:09,304 --> 01:15:10,772
My mouth is already watering.

2051
01:15:11,773 --> 01:15:15,344
Nam-no made three dishes
and finished first.

2052
01:15:15,410 --> 01:15:16,578
-He did.
-Yes.

2053
01:15:16,645 --> 01:15:18,547
-Oh, I made three.
-Will his generation begin?

2054
01:15:18,614 --> 01:15:20,449
ALREADY FORGOT

2055
01:15:20,916 --> 01:15:23,318
1. DANDAN NOODLES

2056
01:15:24,553 --> 01:15:26,588
2. AVOCADO CANAPE

2057
01:15:27,556 --> 01:15:29,858
3. CUCUMBER SALAD

2058
01:15:30,726 --> 01:15:33,996
CHEF YOON NAM-NO'S
RIGHT NOW, IT'S NAM-NO'S GENERATION!

2059
01:15:34,062 --> 01:15:36,832
First try the canape, then the noodles.

2060
01:15:36,899 --> 01:15:38,834
-Canape.
-Then have the cucumber salad

2061
01:15:38,901 --> 01:15:41,136
-like a side dish when you need it.
-When she needs it?

2062
01:15:41,203 --> 01:15:42,371
Yes, that's the appetizer.

2063
01:15:42,437 --> 01:15:44,106
A BIG BITE

2064
01:15:44,907 --> 01:15:46,875
He made that with an avocado.

2065
01:15:46,942 --> 01:15:49,811
-Is that seaweed <i>bugak</i> at the bottom?
-Yes.

2066
01:15:49,878 --> 01:15:51,813
That alone should be flavorful already.

2067
01:15:51,880 --> 01:15:53,582
-Jong-won's <i>bugak.</i>
-You don't seem happy.

2068
01:15:53,815 --> 01:15:55,317
IS IT BAD?

2069
01:15:55,384 --> 01:15:56,351
It's not that.

2070
01:15:56,418 --> 01:15:58,186
I frown when something tastes good.

2071
01:15:58,253 --> 01:16:00,622
AH-HA

2072
01:16:00,689 --> 01:16:02,824
She frowns when something is good.

2073
01:16:04,426 --> 01:16:05,694
Did you add wasabi?

2074
01:16:05,761 --> 01:16:09,164
<i>Yes, to add a bit of spice,</i>
<i>and some avocado oil.</i>

2075
01:16:09,231 --> 01:16:10,999
I see. Avocado oil.

2076
01:16:11,066 --> 01:16:13,235
It feels like a bar snack.

2077
01:16:13,302 --> 01:16:15,270
It can be a bar snack,

2078
01:16:15,337 --> 01:16:17,172
or brunch, whatever you want it to be.

2079
01:16:17,239 --> 01:16:19,708
-Right.
-I just mashed some stuff together.

2080
01:16:20,742 --> 01:16:22,044
It doesn't suit mornings.

2081
01:16:23,078 --> 01:16:25,180
-He called it a canape.
-I should've thought it through.

2082
01:16:25,847 --> 01:16:28,150
It's really good.

2083
01:16:28,216 --> 01:16:31,019
<i>Bugak</i> is already seasoned.

2084
01:16:31,086 --> 01:16:33,755
Chef Jong-won's <i>bugak</i>
is playing a big role today.

2085
01:16:33,822 --> 01:16:35,457
-They're making use of it.
-It's good.

2086
01:16:35,524 --> 01:16:38,093
What was your intention behind this <i>bugak?</i>

2087
01:16:38,160 --> 01:16:41,229
"<i>Bugak</i>" is important in itself,

2088
01:16:41,296 --> 01:16:43,498
but I wanted to "bring out"
other ingredients.

2089
01:16:44,232 --> 01:16:45,367
A COMEDIAN

2090
01:16:45,434 --> 01:16:46,735
<i>Bugak</i> "brings out" other ingredients.

2091
01:16:46,802 --> 01:16:49,004
Sung-jun issues a warning.

2092
01:16:49,071 --> 01:16:49,938
Dandan noodles.

2093
01:16:50,739 --> 01:16:52,307
There's chili oil down there.

2094
01:16:52,374 --> 01:16:54,376
-Is this burrata?
-Burrata.

2095
01:16:54,443 --> 01:16:56,311
It is, but I only used the creamy center.

2096
01:16:56,378 --> 01:16:58,680
I wanted you to enjoy the smooth texture.

2097
01:16:58,747 --> 01:17:00,215
-Sounds good.
-It looks soft.

2098
01:17:00,282 --> 01:17:02,150
I feel like I just became rich.

2099
01:17:02,651 --> 01:17:05,320
-Whoa.
-Those are just regular <i>ramyeon </i>noodles.

2100
01:17:05,387 --> 01:17:06,788
-Yes, regular <i>ramyeon.</i>
-Yes.

2101
01:17:06,855 --> 01:17:09,024
I still don't get
why he made four servings.

2102
01:17:09,091 --> 01:17:10,726
Did you serve all of it?

2103
01:17:10,792 --> 01:17:12,694
I left mine on the side.

2104
01:17:12,761 --> 01:17:14,930
-Over there?
-This is just one serving.

2105
01:17:14,997 --> 01:17:16,765
He had about a bag while tasting it.

2106
01:17:17,866 --> 01:17:19,067
SNIFF

2107
01:17:19,134 --> 01:17:19,968
What is it?

2108
01:17:20,035 --> 01:17:21,370
Does it smell good?

2109
01:17:21,436 --> 01:17:24,172
-It smells…
-It smells how?

2110
01:17:24,239 --> 01:17:25,307
…so delicious.

2111
01:17:27,843 --> 01:17:29,044
Does it smell like dandan noodles?

2112
01:17:29,111 --> 01:17:30,312
TRUSTS HIM AND TAKES A BIG BITE

2113
01:17:30,379 --> 01:17:33,315
-It's made with peanuts, so probably.
-It looks good.

2114
01:17:33,382 --> 01:17:35,384
She's frowning again because it's so good.

2115
01:17:35,684 --> 01:17:37,586
DEPRESSED, PROUD

2116
01:17:37,653 --> 01:17:39,688
What's it like?

2117
01:17:39,755 --> 01:17:42,424
THINKING…

2118
01:17:42,491 --> 01:17:44,159
But you can't eat more than a bite.

2119
01:17:44,593 --> 01:17:46,728
A SUDDEN ATTACK(?)

2120
01:17:46,795 --> 01:17:49,631
-Did it taste too intense?
-It's intense.

2121
01:17:49,698 --> 01:17:53,602
You feel happy with the first bite,
but it's a huge amount of happiness.

2122
01:17:54,569 --> 01:17:56,138
-Wait, no.
-What is it?

2123
01:17:56,204 --> 01:17:58,206
The spiciness just kicked in.

2124
01:17:58,273 --> 01:17:59,408
I can go back for more.

2125
01:17:59,474 --> 01:18:00,942
You need that spiciness.

2126
01:18:01,009 --> 01:18:03,111
-It was the chili oil.
-Chili oil.

2127
01:18:03,178 --> 01:18:04,179
<i>It hit me toward the end.</i>

2128
01:18:04,246 --> 01:18:06,181
A DASH OF FLAVOR VARIATION

2129
01:18:06,248 --> 01:18:08,216
-It's a fancy dish.
-One more bite.

2130
01:18:08,283 --> 01:18:11,853
-Try the cucumber salad too.
-A refreshing bite.

2131
01:18:11,920 --> 01:18:14,322
-And enjoy the sourness.
-So you keep eating it.

2132
01:18:14,389 --> 01:18:17,259
I thought it'd be too dry
since it didn't look too saucy.

2133
01:18:17,325 --> 01:18:18,393
It's really delicious.

2134
01:18:18,460 --> 01:18:19,561
The last dish.

2135
01:18:20,662 --> 01:18:22,264
This is like a palate cleanser?

2136
01:18:23,098 --> 01:18:23,932
Gosh.

2137
01:18:24,499 --> 01:18:25,967
Cucumbers smell so good.

2138
01:18:26,034 --> 01:18:28,003
The moment I smelled it,

2139
01:18:28,070 --> 01:18:30,872
it reminded me of cold cucumber soup.

2140
01:18:30,939 --> 01:18:32,174
-Is it like that?
-Yes.

2141
01:18:32,240 --> 01:18:33,909
The mix must be perfect.

2142
01:18:33,975 --> 01:18:36,278
Cold cucumber soup is great in summer.

2143
01:18:38,113 --> 01:18:39,347
You're so witty.

2144
01:18:39,414 --> 01:18:40,982
THE PRINCESS SHOOTS OUT HEARTS

2145
01:18:41,049 --> 01:18:43,251
HOLDING HIM IN CHECK?

2146
01:18:43,318 --> 01:18:45,754
It refreshes my mouth in an instant.

2147
01:18:46,054 --> 01:18:48,123
FRESH FLAVORS OF CUCUMBERS AND TOMATOES

2148
01:18:48,190 --> 01:18:50,192
I'm sure there's a reason why he made it.

2149
01:18:50,258 --> 01:18:51,293
EXCITED NAM-NO

2150
01:18:51,359 --> 01:18:55,097
You pressed down on the cucumbers
and tomatoes back there, right?

2151
01:18:55,163 --> 01:18:57,299
How does that help?

2152
01:18:57,365 --> 01:18:59,000
I wanted to release its juice

2153
01:18:59,067 --> 01:19:02,137
and salt it to let it draw out the water.

2154
01:19:02,204 --> 01:19:04,639
So it can get seasoned
in a short period of time.

2155
01:19:04,706 --> 01:19:06,508
To salt it in a short period of time.

2156
01:19:06,575 --> 01:19:08,877
I guess that's how he did it so quickly.

2157
01:19:08,944 --> 01:19:12,013
-It's so good.
-I see.

2158
01:19:12,080 --> 01:19:14,649
There are other dishes,
so why don't we stop for now?

2159
01:19:14,716 --> 01:19:16,785
Next, Chef Eun-yeong's dish…

2160
01:19:16,852 --> 01:19:18,987
<i>MicrowaGee, Gee, Gee, Gee</i>

2161
01:19:19,454 --> 01:19:22,591
MAPO TOFU MADE WITH A MICROWAVE

2162
01:19:23,358 --> 01:19:26,461
BLUEBERRY BINGSU
(MADE WITH AN IMMERSION BLENDER)

2163
01:19:28,130 --> 01:19:30,999
CHEF PARK EUN-YEONG'S MICROWAGEE

2164
01:19:31,800 --> 01:19:34,469
That egg holds the key.

2165
01:19:34,536 --> 01:19:37,472
It's still hot at the bottom,
so you can cook the egg in the heat.

2166
01:19:37,539 --> 01:19:38,940
It's cooked.

2167
01:19:39,007 --> 01:19:39,841
It's slightly cooked.

2168
01:19:39,908 --> 01:19:41,777
-Some time has passed.
-While she waited?

2169
01:19:41,843 --> 01:19:44,246
-It's perfect.
-It looks perfect?

2170
01:19:44,479 --> 01:19:45,914
THE CHINESE SISTER FEELS PROUD

2171
01:19:45,981 --> 01:19:47,349
She calculated everything.

2172
01:19:47,415 --> 01:19:48,950
I wonder what it's like.

2173
01:19:49,017 --> 01:19:51,486
-Will it taste like mapo tofu?
-Right?

2174
01:19:52,420 --> 01:19:54,222
YUM

2175
01:19:54,956 --> 01:19:56,224
SO HOT

2176
01:19:56,558 --> 01:19:58,059
OVERLY IMMERSED

2177
01:19:58,293 --> 01:20:00,162
OH, GOSH

2178
01:20:00,228 --> 01:20:02,831
-You were inconsiderate.
-Oh, no.

2179
01:20:02,898 --> 01:20:04,800
What have you done to my Sooyoung?

2180
01:20:04,866 --> 01:20:06,201
So inconsiderate.

2181
01:20:08,837 --> 01:20:10,605
THIS IS WHAT I WANTED, GEE

2182
01:20:10,672 --> 01:20:12,908
So it's both hot and delicious?

2183
01:20:12,974 --> 01:20:15,710
-Is it spicy?
-Just enough to be delicious.

2184
01:20:15,777 --> 01:20:16,878
-Is it spicy?
-Yes.

2185
01:20:16,945 --> 01:20:20,849
I've been having trouble
trying to get rid of the rice cake,

2186
01:20:20,916 --> 01:20:24,486
and I had no idea
you'd put it into mapo tofu.

2187
01:20:24,553 --> 01:20:26,454
Many people eat it with rice,

2188
01:20:26,521 --> 01:20:28,557
but I didn't think
you would've had it with rice cakes.

2189
01:20:28,623 --> 01:20:31,860
I wanted to serve you a nice dish
with a mix of carbs and protein,

2190
01:20:31,927 --> 01:20:33,895
<i>a perfect meal, so to speak.</i>

2191
01:20:33,962 --> 01:20:36,498
So you used rice cakes
instead of serving rice?

2192
01:20:37,566 --> 01:20:40,535
You ended up giving
her unhinged rice cakes a makeover.

2193
01:20:40,602 --> 01:20:43,705
-It looks hot.
-She's fighting heat with heat.

2194
01:20:43,772 --> 01:20:46,141
If it's that hot,
why can't you just blow on it?

2195
01:20:46,208 --> 01:20:48,210
-There's a reason.
-You might burn your mouth.

2196
01:20:48,276 --> 01:20:50,412
-Tofu has a fluffy texture,
-Yes.

2197
01:20:50,478 --> 01:20:52,414
-…and so do eggs.
-True.

2198
01:20:52,480 --> 01:20:55,283
Also, the sauce is hot right now,

2199
01:20:55,350 --> 01:20:58,887
-and I like to enjoy it while it's hot.
-So you like your food hot?

2200
01:20:58,954 --> 01:21:02,591
Also, rice cakes can contain heat inside.

2201
01:21:02,657 --> 01:21:04,826
Yes, if you eat rice cakes the wrong way,

2202
01:21:04,893 --> 01:21:05,861
you might even lose a tooth.

2203
01:21:05,927 --> 01:21:07,696
-A tooth?
-You can lose a tooth.

2204
01:21:07,762 --> 01:21:09,331
It really happens.

2205
01:21:09,397 --> 01:21:10,565
GOOD GRIEF

2206
01:21:10,632 --> 01:21:12,267
There's always someone like that
in a country village.

2207
01:21:12,701 --> 01:21:15,737
WHAT KIND OF COUNTRYSIDE
IS HE TALKING ABOUT?

2208
01:21:16,104 --> 01:21:19,107
CONTINUES TO EAT
DESPITE THE RISK OF LOSING HER TEETH(?)

2209
01:21:19,174 --> 01:21:22,177
-This is going to be hard.
-She keeps eating it.

2210
01:21:22,244 --> 01:21:24,813
I thought she'd stop
because it was too hot.

2211
01:21:24,880 --> 01:21:27,816
While I'm eating this scorching hot dish,

2212
01:21:27,883 --> 01:21:29,084
I can still see this.

2213
01:21:29,150 --> 01:21:31,086
-Blueberry <i>bingsu.</i>
-It must be exciting.

2214
01:21:31,152 --> 01:21:33,388
It's exciting and nice to see it there.

2215
01:21:33,455 --> 01:21:35,557
-Your mouth must feel hot.
-The temperature difference.

2216
01:21:35,624 --> 01:21:38,326
Next, blueberry <i>bingsu.</i>

2217
01:21:38,927 --> 01:21:40,462
It'll refresh your mouth.

2218
01:21:41,363 --> 01:21:42,330
And cool it down.

2219
01:21:43,732 --> 01:21:45,600
Will that be the decisive factor?

2220
01:21:46,401 --> 01:21:49,404
-She just likes desserts.
-She likes desserts.

2221
01:21:49,471 --> 01:21:51,973
Sooyoung always needs a dessert.

2222
01:21:52,040 --> 01:21:53,041
Nice try, Nam-no.

2223
01:21:53,108 --> 01:21:54,776
I want to see this thing for sale.

2224
01:21:55,443 --> 01:21:56,978
Is it that good?

2225
01:21:57,045 --> 01:21:58,580
It's simple, so make it at home.

2226
01:21:58,647 --> 01:21:59,881
Just blend everything together.

2227
01:21:59,948 --> 01:22:00,849
INHALES

2228
01:22:00,916 --> 01:22:02,984
I can't be bothered to wash the blender.

2229
01:22:03,218 --> 01:22:05,620
UNDERSTANDABLE

2230
01:22:05,687 --> 01:22:07,956
Because of the cream cheese,

2231
01:22:08,023 --> 01:22:10,859
I find myself thinking,
"Is it less refreshing?"

2232
01:22:10,926 --> 01:22:13,628
But then a piece of peach gets right in.

2233
01:22:13,695 --> 01:22:15,597
It's very refreshing and delicious.

2234
01:22:15,664 --> 01:22:18,466
And because of that,
this is a great dish to eat

2235
01:22:18,533 --> 01:22:21,336
-along with this. The balance is great.
-The balance must be great.

2236
01:22:21,636 --> 01:22:23,305
BOTH MEALS RECEIVE GREAT COMPLIMENTS

2237
01:22:23,371 --> 01:22:25,340
It's so tough to choose.

2238
01:22:25,407 --> 01:22:29,544
Now, let's try Chef Nam-no's dish first.

2239
01:22:29,611 --> 01:22:30,445
MMM

2240
01:22:31,379 --> 01:22:33,415
It's mild and delicious. And nutty.

2241
01:22:33,481 --> 01:22:35,884
Mild, delicious, and nutty.

2242
01:22:35,951 --> 01:22:37,652
Just eating this will fill me up.

2243
01:22:37,719 --> 01:22:38,820
Really?

2244
01:22:41,589 --> 01:22:42,991
Why do you have so much left?

2245
01:22:43,058 --> 01:22:44,726
WANT SOME?

2246
01:22:44,793 --> 01:22:47,462
It wouldn't have been
as good without the chili oil.

2247
01:22:47,862 --> 01:22:52,067
OR EAT IT WITH REFRESHING CUCUMBER SALAD

2248
01:22:52,667 --> 01:22:54,436
DECIDED TO JOIN HIM

2249
01:22:56,237 --> 01:22:57,472
It's good.

2250
01:22:57,539 --> 01:22:58,740
RESPONDS IMMEDIATELY

2251
01:22:58,807 --> 01:22:59,808
This is good.

2252
01:23:00,475 --> 01:23:03,278
I really want to know the recipe.

2253
01:23:03,345 --> 01:23:05,046
It has a bang at the end.

2254
01:23:05,113 --> 01:23:08,316
-It's so good.
-Really?

2255
01:23:08,383 --> 01:23:10,652
The sauce ratio is very easy.

2256
01:23:10,719 --> 01:23:13,455
My kids would love this.

2257
01:23:13,955 --> 01:23:16,424
<i>I have to take the recipe from Nam-no.</i>

2258
01:23:16,491 --> 01:23:17,692
<i>Is that hard to make?</i>

2259
01:23:17,759 --> 01:23:19,327
<i>No, it's just one each.</i>

2260
01:23:19,394 --> 01:23:21,997
<i>-Peanut butter. Soy sauce.</i>
<i>-Soy sauce.</i>

2261
01:23:22,063 --> 01:23:23,898
<i>-Oyster sauce, sugar.</i>
<i>-Oyster sauce, sugar.</i>

2262
01:23:23,965 --> 01:23:24,833
<i>And sesame oil.</i>

2263
01:23:24,899 --> 01:23:26,401
It's so good.

2264
01:23:26,468 --> 01:23:29,771
It's a nice dish to make for the summer.

2265
01:23:29,838 --> 01:23:32,207
It's like cold <i>ramyeon.</i>

2266
01:23:32,273 --> 01:23:33,441
He mixed the tomatoes

2267
01:23:33,508 --> 01:23:37,545
with cucumber, including the juice,

2268
01:23:37,612 --> 01:23:40,448
and that brought out the umami.
It's so good.

2269
01:23:40,515 --> 01:23:41,449
It's good.

2270
01:23:41,516 --> 01:23:43,118
-Thank you.
-"It's good."

2271
01:23:43,184 --> 01:23:45,687
Next, Chef Eun-yeong's dish.

2272
01:23:46,187 --> 01:23:47,889
MicrowaGee.

2273
01:23:49,057 --> 01:23:52,093
It's not like mapo tofu,
but more like <i>tteokbokki.</i>

2274
01:23:52,160 --> 01:23:54,396
EYES OPENED WIDE

2275
01:23:54,462 --> 01:23:58,099
-It tastes pleasantly spicy.
-It does.

2276
01:23:58,166 --> 01:24:00,001
-It's so good.
-It's so good.

2277
01:24:00,068 --> 01:24:04,039
-Like Chinese-style brisket <i>tteokbokki.</i>
-It's sweet.

2278
01:24:04,105 --> 01:24:07,409
But when the tofu melts,
it also feels like a healthy dish.

2279
01:24:07,475 --> 01:24:09,978
I want to eat something like this
while watching <i>mukbang</i> at night.

2280
01:24:10,045 --> 01:24:12,047
NODDING

2281
01:24:12,113 --> 01:24:15,016
It would be easy on your stomach
even if you eat it late at night.

2282
01:24:15,083 --> 01:24:18,386
-It's such a mild mapo tofu.
-It wouldn't even make you fat.

2283
01:24:18,453 --> 01:24:21,189
It would be great
if this could be sold as a meal kit,

2284
01:24:21,256 --> 01:24:23,925
-something you can microwave and eat.
-Yes.

2285
01:24:23,992 --> 01:24:28,329
You can only call the dish mapo tofu
if you use <i>doubanjiang</i>.

2286
01:24:28,396 --> 01:24:31,666
People usually don't have that,
but they'll have gochujang.

2287
01:24:31,733 --> 01:24:34,035
<i>So try making it with gochujang as I did.</i>

2288
01:24:34,102 --> 01:24:36,538
-I think that suits our palate better.
-Right.

2289
01:24:36,604 --> 01:24:38,339
-Please try the dessert.
-Okay.

2290
01:24:41,209 --> 01:24:42,143
MMM♥

2291
01:24:42,944 --> 01:24:45,013
-It's a perfect way to wrap up the meal.
-It is.

2292
01:24:45,080 --> 01:24:46,514
A perfect ending.

2293
01:24:46,581 --> 01:24:48,083
It's a nice and mild finish.

2294
01:24:48,149 --> 01:24:50,718
-It doesn't make you feel guilty either.
-Desserts are important.

2295
01:24:50,785 --> 01:24:52,654
What now? You're in trouble.

2296
01:24:52,720 --> 01:24:54,055
FEELS GUILTY(?) OVER HER CHOICE

2297
01:24:54,122 --> 01:24:56,724
It's a really difficult decision.

2298
01:24:56,791 --> 01:24:57,759
You have lots.

2299
01:24:57,826 --> 01:24:59,094
-Make a decision.
-It's been a while.

2300
01:24:59,160 --> 01:25:00,328
<i>Press one for Eun-yeong,</i>

2301
01:25:01,496 --> 01:25:02,997
<i>or press two for Nam-no.</i>

2302
01:25:03,832 --> 01:25:04,999
Make your decision

2303
01:25:05,066 --> 01:25:06,601
and press the button!

2304
01:25:07,368 --> 01:25:09,971
It'll be a fatal blow
to whoever doesn't get a star.

2305
01:25:10,038 --> 01:25:11,072
They both did so well.

2306
01:25:12,173 --> 01:25:14,709
-They did a great job.
-I'm sorry.

2307
01:25:15,910 --> 01:25:17,579
-I'm sorry.
-Did you press it?

2308
01:25:17,645 --> 01:25:18,546
-Yes.
-You did?

2309
01:25:18,913 --> 01:25:21,816
SHE CHOSE JUST ONE PERSON
AFTER A LOT OF THOUGHT

2310
01:25:21,883 --> 01:25:24,586
Let's find out
who Sooyoung chose. Show us.

2311
01:25:25,787 --> 01:25:28,756
<i>Don't Skip Meals</i>
<i>Because You Can't Be Bothered</i>

2312
01:25:28,823 --> 01:25:33,261
If Eun-yeong wins,
she'll break her four-loss streak.

2313
01:25:33,328 --> 01:25:36,898
If Nam-no wins,
he'll begin his winning streak.

2314
01:25:36,965 --> 01:25:39,868
Who did Sooyoung choose?

2315
01:25:40,368 --> 01:25:42,704
A dish she can make
even when she can't be bothered.

2316
01:25:42,770 --> 01:25:44,139
Which one made that?

2317
01:25:44,672 --> 01:25:45,840
Who's the winner?

2318
01:25:52,680 --> 01:25:54,015
PARK EUN-YEONG WINS

2319
01:25:54,082 --> 01:25:55,517
It's Park Eun-yeong.

2320
01:25:55,583 --> 01:25:57,385
CHEF PARK EUN-YEONG'S MICROWAGEE WINS

2321
01:25:57,452 --> 01:25:58,853
It's Park Eun-yeong.

2322
01:25:58,920 --> 01:26:01,089
Eun-yeong wins the round.

2323
01:26:01,156 --> 01:26:03,858
-She wins this round.
-She just loves desserts.

2324
01:26:03,925 --> 01:26:05,627
She finally breaks her losing streak.

2325
01:26:05,693 --> 01:26:09,998
I'm the type who enjoys the flavors
from typical Korean cuisine.

2326
01:26:10,064 --> 01:26:12,167
When she said it was mapo tofu,

2327
01:26:12,233 --> 01:26:15,170
<i>I thought it'd taste like a Chinese dish.</i>

2328
01:26:15,236 --> 01:26:17,639
-But it tasted a bit like <i>tteokbokki.</i>
-Yes.

2329
01:26:17,705 --> 01:26:22,944
Also, it was a dish I would
actually get around to making at home.

2330
01:26:23,011 --> 01:26:25,213
I'm going to try it.

2331
01:26:25,280 --> 01:26:27,849
-Adding gochujang was the winning move.
-It was.

2332
01:26:27,916 --> 01:26:30,151
It tasted like
something my mom would make.

2333
01:26:30,218 --> 01:26:33,321
-It did.
-Like the mapo tofu our moms would make.

2334
01:26:33,388 --> 01:26:36,257
Also, adding rice cakes
instead of rice was a big win.

2335
01:26:36,324 --> 01:26:38,426
Is Nam-no's generation yet to come?

2336
01:26:38,493 --> 01:26:40,728
-Is it not your generation yet?
-Right?

2337
01:26:40,795 --> 01:26:43,364
I've eaten a hearty amount today,
so I'm fine.

2338
01:26:43,765 --> 01:26:45,466
HOW ADORABLE

2339
01:26:45,533 --> 01:26:47,368
Please put a star on Chef Eun-yeong.

2340
01:26:49,304 --> 01:26:50,772
-Great job.
-Great job.

2341
01:26:50,838 --> 01:26:53,141
This is her sixth win,
and she's back on track.

2342
01:26:53,208 --> 01:26:54,275
Congratulations.

2343
01:26:54,342 --> 01:26:55,810
Congratulations, Eun-yeong.

2344
01:26:56,144 --> 01:26:58,413
NAM-NO'S GENERATION SHALL COME

2345
01:26:58,846 --> 01:27:01,249
Her career has been going strong
ever since her debut.

2346
01:27:01,316 --> 01:27:02,550
Do you feel the generational gap?

2347
01:27:02,617 --> 01:27:03,718
Not really.

2348
01:27:03,785 --> 01:27:05,286
<i>Chef & My Fridge, yaho!</i>

2349
01:27:05,520 --> 01:27:06,454
KNOWS ALL THE MEMES

2350
01:27:06,521 --> 01:27:08,523
The young guns of the show
just shoot right home.

2351
01:27:08,590 --> 01:27:10,792
She said, "Let's go to a karaoke room!"

2352
01:27:10,858 --> 01:27:12,360
You had fun that day, right?

2353
01:27:12,427 --> 01:27:14,229
It was so much fun, Jung-hwa!

2354
01:27:14,462 --> 01:27:15,530
SOCIAL MODE ON

2355
01:27:15,597 --> 01:27:16,965
We present Jung-hwa's fridge!

2356
01:27:17,031 --> 01:27:18,566
I love carrots so much.

2357
01:27:18,633 --> 01:27:19,667
That's a zucchini.

2358
01:27:19,734 --> 01:27:21,169
It's delicious when grilled.

2359
01:27:21,236 --> 01:27:24,472
Let the 15-minute cook-off
for Jung-hwa begin!

2360
01:27:24,806 --> 01:27:27,075
A NEW WORLD OF VEGETABLE DISHES

2361
01:27:27,141 --> 01:27:28,443
<i>Yareu!</i>

2362
01:27:28,509 --> 01:27:30,078
He seems way more confident.

2363
01:27:30,144 --> 01:27:32,113
I'm going to chop everything.

2364
01:27:32,380 --> 01:27:33,948
HIS MOUTH IS STILL ADJUSTING

2365
01:27:34,015 --> 01:27:35,583
It's really good!

2366
01:27:35,650 --> 01:27:36,818
<i>Yareu!</i>

2367
01:27:37,218 --> 01:27:38,386
IF IT'S GOOD, SAY "YAHO!"

2368
01:27:38,620 --> 01:27:40,421
THE FIRST 2 VS. 2 TAG TEAM ROUND

2369
01:27:40,488 --> 01:27:41,489
THE MOST EXTREME TEAMWORK MATCH

2370
01:27:41,556 --> 01:27:42,924
Salt.

2371
01:27:43,224 --> 01:27:44,559
SMALL VOICE, PERFECT TEAMWORK

2372
01:27:44,759 --> 01:27:45,927
THE CHEF AND THE KITCHEN TOOLMAN

2373
01:27:45,994 --> 01:27:47,228
UH! UGH!

2374
01:27:47,428 --> 01:27:48,696
BUT THEIR OPPONENTS ARE…

2375
01:27:48,763 --> 01:27:49,797
That's what I'm talking about!

2376
01:27:49,998 --> 01:27:51,499
…THE LOUD AND CRAZY CHINESE SIBLINGS

2377
01:27:51,566 --> 01:27:52,467
You're cheating.

2378
01:27:52,533 --> 01:27:53,868
They're flustered.

2379
01:27:54,302 --> 01:27:56,404
WHAT A TOTAL MESS

2380
01:27:56,638 --> 01:27:58,006
WHAT WILL HAPPEN IN THE TAG TEAM ROUND?

2381
01:27:58,072 --> 01:27:59,707
<i>Can you call this a team round?</i>

2382
01:28:01,376 --> 01:28:02,710
<i>-Yareu.</i>
<i>-Yareu.</i>

2383
01:28:02,777 --> 01:28:04,946
<i>-Yareu.</i>
<i>-Yareu.</i>

2384
01:28:05,013 --> 01:28:07,882
-Today is the death of <i>yareu</i> as a meme.
-The death.

2385
01:28:17,725 --> 01:28:22,497
Subtitle translation by: Eunsook Youn
